  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5436858/assistant-director-for-mission-assessment": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Mission Assessment",
      "description": "Assistant Director for Mission Assessment Salary $67,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600037 Org University Mission Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Assistant Director is responsible for overseeing the assessment practices, outcomes, and action plans across the University’s five mission departments: the Institute for Vincentian Impact, Campus Ministry, the Vincentian Center for Church and Society, the Office of Mission Initiatives, and the Office of Equity and Inclusion. In alignment with the University’s strategic plan, assessment framework, and data-informed practices, the Assistant Director will support efforts to centralize data collection, operationalize assessment processes, and conduct meaningful analysis to inform program improvement and strategic decision-making. As a collaborative administrator, the Assistant Director assists other departments of the University. This position serves as the Mission sector representative on the University Assessment Committee and contributes to both institutional and Vincentian accreditation efforts. The Assistant Director is also responsible for leading outcomes assessment and establishing both long- and short-term goals for mission-aligned programs, departments, and initiatives. Job Responsibilities Primary Area of Focus: Office of University Mission Support the development, implementation, and oversight of assessment plans across all mission departments in alignment with institutional goals and Mission identity and identified areas of the current strategic plan. Support the creation and tracking of measurable outcomes for programs, events, and initiatives that reflect Catholic and Vincentian values. Manage the build, trainings, maintenance, and effective use of the University’s volunteer management platform, GivePulse, to track service participation and engagement. Oversee all community engagement data collection resources, including Qualtrics, Formstack, GivePulse, and other related tools to support program evaluation and reporting. Lead analyses of qualitative and quantitative data to evaluate program effectiveness, including the administration and analysis of the Catholic Identity and Mission Assessment (CIMA) surveys for new students, graduating seniors, and alumni to inform continuous improvement, and support storytelling of mission impact. Assist in identifying and evaluating community partnerships for mission-aligned service and impact assessment. Collaborate with mission-related departments to prepare and present annual and necessary periodic reports on program performance, including faculty engagement, student participation, demographic data, and retention data. Support University-wide accreditation processes by providing mission-specific data, reports, and documentation as needed. Create centralized tools and processes to streamline data collection, improve accuracy, and ensure consistency across departments. Coordinate and facilitate assessment workshops and training for Mission department staff to build capacity and enhance assessment culture. Represent the Division of Mission on the University Assessment Committee and other committees as assigned. Supervise departmental graduate assistant. Other Responsibilities Support the development of assessment plans for the Office of Student Affairs, assisting in the creation of strategies for data collection by that office, and providing analyses and presentation materials requested, with the explicit approval of the Assistant Vice President for Mission Integration. Assist and perform other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility This position does not supervise any full-time administrative and staff members Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in statistics, social sciences (e.g. Psychology, Sociology etc.), or educational program evaluation and minimum of two years of research experience to demonstrate the ability to model data and to conduct complex analyses. Experience with data coding and documentation. Experience working with databases and reporting. Good knowledge of MS Office. Knowledge of or ability to learn Qualtrics, Formstack, GivePulse, and other related tools to support program evaluation and reporting. Demonstrated ability using statistical and data presentation software, (SPSS and MS PowerBI preferred). Detail-oriented with strong problem solving and analytical skills. Strong communication skills [oral/written] with the ability to communicate findings through reports and presentations to stakeholders with varying level of technical knowledge. Comfortable presenting to large groups and/or to high level stakeholders. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to develop and maintain positive and productive working relationships. Ability to work independently and collaboratively with excellent organizational and time management skills. Experience successfully leading multiple projects simultaneously to meet tight timelines. Additional Eligibility Qualifications: A candidate must accept and exemplify the teachings of the Catholic Church on matters of faith and morals in all that concerns their employment and presence at St. John's University. Preferred: Experience in a higher education environment. Proficient writing reports in APA format. Strong interest in poverty alleviation, service, and social justice. Supplemental Information Work Environment This job operates in a professional office environment. This role routinely uses standard office equipment such as personal computers and printers. Physical Demands There are no unique physical demands that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Environmental Conditions are typically representative of a safe working environment, free of any unique conditions (e.g. noise, fumes, odors, gases, significant amounts of dust, hazards) Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. This position may be hybrid eligible, subject to university policy 130. Travel Travel is primarily local and may include visits to the other NY campuses. This position is subject to a comprehensive background screen, with employment contingent upon satisfactory results. Compensation is commensurate with your qualifications and experience and contingent upon the departmental budget. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5442911/adjunct-instructor-aquatic-ecology-lecture-and-laboratory": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor – Aquatic Ecology (Lecture and Laboratory)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor – Aquatic Ecology (Lecture and Laboratory) Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number TF 00-00 Org Biology Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits Questions St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Hiring Rate $12,621.00 Division/Department Information This course serves undergraduate students in both the Biological Sciences (Department of Biological Sciences) and Environmental Sciences programs. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment where students, faculty, and staff from all backgrounds can thrive. Our programs promote equitable access to educational and research opportunities, incorporate diverse perspectives into the curriculum, and cultivate a sense of belonging across the scientific community. Through these efforts, we prepare future scientists to address complex biological and environmental challenges in an increasingly diverse world. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities We seek an enthusiastic Adjunct Instructor to teach Aquatic Ecology, including both lecture and laboratory components. The successful candidate will have a strong background in aquatic ecology and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Responsibilities include: Teaching two 1.5-hour lectures and one 4-hour laboratory session each week. Delivering instructions on aquatic ecosystem dynamics, water quality assessment, and the ecology and behavior of aquatic organisms. Maintaining a safe, engaging, and inclusive learning environment. Assessing student performance and submitting grades in accordance with university policies. Updating course materials as appropriate while building upon existing syllabi, lectures, laboratory exercises, and field activities provided by the department. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications Master's degree or Ph.D. in Ecology, Environmental Science, Aquatic Ecology, or a closely related field. Previous undergraduate teaching experience is preferred. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Supplemental Information Application Process Interested candidates should submit a curriculum vitae (or résumé) and the names and contact information of three professional references by September 15, 2026. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Laura Schramm, Director of Environmental Sciences, at Schramml@stjohns.edu . Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have a Master's degree or Ph.D in Ecology, Environmental Science, Aquatic Ecology, or a related field? Yes No Required Question Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5448044/accommodations-specialist": {
      "title": "Accommodations Specialist",
      "description": "Accommodations Specialist Salary $66,300.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600044 Org Office of Student Affairs Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John's University's Office of Disability Services is seeking a dynamic and passionate individual to serve as a full-time in-person Learning Specialist. The Learning Specialist works directly with students registered with the office to provide individualized support and accommodations, fostering an inclusive learning environment that promotes academic success and personal growth. The Learning Specialist performs educational, instructional, and administrative work associated with ensuring compliance with applicable policies and laws. The Office of Disability Services (ODS) is part of the Department of Student Wellness at St. John’s University. The Department of Student Wellness takes an integrated approach to wellness, consisting of Student Health Services, Wellness Education and Prevention, the Center for Counseling and Consultation (CCC), the Office of Disability Services (ODS), Campus Recreation (CREC), and Sexual Violence Outreach, Awareness, and Response (SOAR). Job Responsibilities Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Reviews/evaluates diagnostic information and documentation of student learning disabilities; determines eligibility for protection under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), Section 504, and other applicable legislation; Determines reasonable accommodation or course substitution; consults with students, faculty, administrators, and other campus personnel regarding students' instructional needs, the status of disability, and reasonable accommodations; Develop customized accommodations in collaboration with students based on assessment results and documentation of disabilities. Assist in the coordination and implementation of accommodations, such as extended test time, note-taking support, accessible materials, and assistive technology. Provide ongoing support and guidance to students to implement and utilize accommodations effectively. Develop and deliver workshops, seminars, and training sessions for students, faculty, and staff on topics related to learning disabilities, inclusive teaching practices, and assistive technology. Collaborate with faculty to promote awareness of diverse learning needs and effective instructional strategies to support students with disabilities. Research and compile resources, including academic support services, community resources, and assistive technology tools, to enhance student learning and success. Maintain an up-to-date database of resources and referral networks for students with disabilities. Provide guidance and recommendations for the acquisition of assistive technology and learning resources. Collaborate with academic advisors, counselors, and other support services to ensure holistic support for students' academic and personal success. Participates in college, division, department meetings, events and training as recommended and approved by supervisor. Participates in professional development opportunities, college committees, work groups and task forces, and other professional organizations as approved by supervisor. Other duties as assigned. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Education and Experience: Master’s degree in special education, Psychology, Counseling, or related fields. Experience working with individuals with disabilities in an educational or support services setting. Knowledge of disability laws and regulations, including the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build rapport and collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders. Commitment to promoting diversity, equity, and inclusion in higher education. Experience with assistive technologies and adaptive learning strategies. Ability to maintain effective, collaborative working relationships with internal and external colleagues and constituents. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Strong written and oral communication skills Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to FERPA regulations. Experience serving diverse populations and a demonstrated commitment to equity. Strong ability to consult and collaborate with others. Preferred Education and Experience: Certification as a Learning Disability Specialist or similar credential Experience with assistive technology and accessible design principles Experience in program development, workshop facilitation, or training delivery. Knowledge of universal design for learning (UDL) principles and instructional design methodologies Supplemental Information Work Environment This position operates in a professional office environment. This position is required to use standard office equipment such as personal computers, printers, etc. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This position is a full-time, in-person position. Typical hours are Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., with the expectation for a flex schedule of two or three days to accommodate evening appointments and programs. This position occasionally requires extended hours and weekend work. Travel when appropriate and requested. Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5458038/adjunct-faculty-position-school-of-education": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Position - School of Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Position - School of Education Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600059 Org The School of Education Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Adjunct Faculty Position - School of Education St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Department: Multiple Departments of the School of Education Specific Job Title: Adjunct Faculty Reports to: Department Chairpersons Campus: Queens Job Summary: Multiple departments within the School of Education at St. John’s University seek applicants for adjunct faculty positions. The needs of the departments will determine the courses. The usual needs for each department are noted below. Administrative and Instructional Leadership: Seeking candidates with experience as school building and district leaders or higher education leadership experience. Ability to teach leadership preparation courses or doctoral courses in theory, technology, and culturally responsive pedagogy. Counselor Education: Seeking candidates with a strong Counselor Identity, preferably graduates of Counselor Education programs, who could teach in any of the eight CACREP core areas, or within the school counseling or clinical mental health counseling specialization courses. A preferred qualification is a Doctoral Degree from a CACREP-accredited Counselor Education program or related field. Curriculum and Instruction: Seeking candidates to teach foundations of education, special education, human learning and development, methodology for various disciplines, instructional technology, human relations and multiculturalism, classroom management, art and music in inclusive settings, and assessment. Education Specialties: Seeking candidates with terminal degrees, preparation, teaching experience, and certification in one or more of the following areas: Special Education, PK-12. TESOL (ENL), PK-12, Literacy, PK-12, Literacy Online Doctoral level. Knowledge and skill in online CANVAS preferred. Job Responsibilities The primary responsibility for this position is teaching undergraduate and/or graduate students pursuing degrees leading to state certification. Classes are in person (at the address: 8000 Utopia Parkway, Queens, NY 11439) and online, both synchronously and asynchronously. For asynchronous classes, a certificate is required. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Education: Candidates must have a master’s or doctoral degree within the field of the applicable department. Required Teaching Experience: Candidates should have at least three years of classroom teaching or professional counseling experience, with a preference for candidates fully certified in their area of expertise. Required Skills and Characteristics: Public speaking and teaching; technology skills to include administrative functions (e.g. email, Microsoft Office products, videoconferencing software) and teaching functions (e.g. learning management systems, interactive teaching technologies) Supplemental Information The School of Education: The School of Education offers doctoral degree (i.e., Ed.D. and Ph.D.) programs and 43 master’s degree programs that accommodate career changers, field changers, and those who seek expertise and/or certification in the areas of Adolescent Education, Childhood Education, Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Early Childhood Education, Literacy, School Building Leadership, School Counseling, Special Education, and TESOL. Our programs are designed to be flexible, with online and traditional schedules. Department of Administrative and Instructional Leadership: The Department of Administrative and Instructional Leadership offers master’s and advanced certificates in school building/district leadership and educational doctorates in instructional leadership and administration and supervision. The master’s and advanced certificates are offered online, while the Ed.D. programs are delivered with hybrid and online course options. All synchronous courses are offered in the evening after 5 PM. Department of Counselor Education: The Department of Counselor Education offers master’s degrees and advanced certificates in School Counseling and Clinical Mental Health Counseling. The advanced certificate in school counseling is offered online, and all other programs are offered on the Queens campus with online course options. All programs are offered in the evenings after 5 PM. Department of Curriculum and Instruction: The Department of Curriculum and Instruction offers bachelor’s and master’s degrees in childhood and adolescent education and a doctoral degree in curriculum and instruction. The department also offers middle school extension advanced certificates. Courses are offered on the Queens campus and online during the day and evening. Department of Education Specialties: The Department of Education Specialties offers in-person, hybrid and online master’s degrees and advanced certificates in Literacy PK-12, Special Education, PK-12, and TESOL, PK-12. An online Ph.D. in Literacy is offered. Dual certification MS programs are also offered in TESOL/Special Education, Literacy/TESOL, and Special Education/Literacy. Application Process: Applications will be accepted until positions are filled. Please submit your letter of interest and CV online as ONE pdf file. Salary: In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, For the 2026-2027 academic year, the minimum credit hour rate for adjunct faculty members shall be as follows: Adjunct Professor $2,215 Adjunct Associate Professor $2,009 Adjunct Assistant Professor $1,906 Adjunct Instructor $1,803 *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer* Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer.All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5464751/assistant-athletics-director-facilities-and-operations": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletics Director Facilities and Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Athletics Director Facilities and Operations Salary $72,700.00 - $75,300.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600064 Org Athletic Facilities Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Assistant Athletic Director for Facilities and Operations reports to the Deputy Athletic Director. This person leads the day-to-day management of 8 athletic facilities, including maintenance scheduling, and scheduling allocation for athletic programs, departmental needs, and approved campus events. This position is responsible for arranging and supervising all events taking place in any athletic fields including events held in athletic facilities by non-athletic groups and outside organizations and the maintenance and upkeep of the athletic fields including day to day interactions with the following departments: Public Safety, Facility Services, Fir Food Services, Grounds, IT/Telecommunications etc. is a requirement and a duty. Oversee all aspects of Division 1 intercollegiate competitions and event operations. Job Responsibilities •Manage game operations, ensuring game practices and services are meeting the needs and addressing the needs of coaches, student-athletes, visiting teams, officials, and fans. •Manage the scheduling of practices and events for 17 Division 1 sports teams. Provide comprehensive oversight of complicated process with teams sharing multiple locations and training and competing nearly year round. •Provide management and oversight of the department's staff including Athletics Event Manager 4 graduate assistants, 4-5 interns and 10-15 student workers, and 80 event staffers including hiring training, and payroll. •Maintain and upkeep all electronic equipment: scoreboards, LED message boards, clock and sound equipment including the department's music laptops •Oversee athletic department passenger vans to include: maintain accurate booking of vehicles, ensure all drivers are formally approved to drive by the University, track and schedule maintenance of vehicles, preserve cleanliness of van pool, enforce van use policies, review and update van policies annually •Communicate departmental needs and coordinate efforts with Conference Services, Special Events, Facilities Services, Maintenance, Grounds, Night Cleaners, Purchasing, IT/Telecommunications, Food Services, Public Safety, Fire Safety and Environmental Safety departments •Develop daily work order log, generate and track maintenance work tickets, work orders, security key lock work orders, and telephone service requests •Work in conjunction with University Facilities and Grounds to ensure all outside facilities including: Belson Stadium, Belson Press Box, Kaiser Stadium, DaSilva Track & Field, DaSilva Press Box, Softball Field, and Tennis Courts are ready for practice and competition •Help oversee facilities planning, renovations, special facilities projects and capital planning •Manage the planning, and coordination of event operations before, during, and after all athletic events. •Determine all logistical needs and communicate and coordinate necessary services for campus public safety, marketing/Learfield IMG, ticketing & ushering, sports information, concessions, IT, and university facilities/grounds department. •Coordinate pre-season meetings with all coaches, assistant coaches and to all appropriate departments, vendors and others to ensure necessary levels of staffing coverage and overall event understanding. •Manage and coordinate the operations for TV production staff during televised events on campus. Create and assist in the development of event policies and procedures for staff and guests. •Ensure the highest level of service by identifying and communicating solutions to problems. •The role requires frequent travel to athletic facilities, coordination with multiple departments, and the ability to manage high-pressure event environments. It involves both administrative oversight and hands-on operational management •Performs other duties as assigned. Provide management and oversight of the department's staff including Athletics Event Manager 4 graduate assistants, 4-5 interns and 10-15 student workers, and 80 event staffers including hiring training, and payroll. Competencies, Education, Experience Strong organization, relationship management and communication skills. Ability to multi task and provide outstanding service to coaches and staff members. •Bachelor's degree and 8-10 years related experience or training, or equivalent combination of education and experience. •List licenses or certifications required/preferred. •Bachelors' degree required, Masters degree preferred in related field •2-4 years of experience in athletic operations and facilities at the collegiate level •Supervisory experience preferred •Strong communication and interpersonal skills •Exceptional multi-tasking skills needed •Valid Driver's License •Knowledge of MS Office (MS Word, MS Excel, MS PowerPoint) required Supplemental Information This position operates in a professional office environment as well as indoor and outdoor athletic facilities. Work is performed in stadiums, arenas, athletic fields, practice facilities, event spaces, and administrative offices. The position regularly uses computers, printers, telephones, electronic event equipment, scoreboards, communication devices, and other standard office and event management tools. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. While performing the duties of this position, the employee is regularly required to move equipment. The employee is frequently required to climb stairs, bend, stoop, kneel, reach, and transport equipment and event materials. The employee must occasionally lift, move, push, or carry objects. Environmental Conditions Wok may require being exposed to unique conditions on athletic fields. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work For example: days and hours of work are full time Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. This position regularly requires long hours and weekend work. Travel Travel to off campus events and competitions on occasion. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5464772/academic-advisor": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor Salary $75,000.00 - $79,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600067 Org Center for Student Success Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary This position, Academic Advisor reporting to the Associate Director of Academic Advising, advises undergraduate students concerning the academic requirements for their chosen program. This position is responsible for assisting with courses election and the course registration process. This position provides information on and refers students to university resources that can assist in meeting their needs or solving problems; communicates accurate and timely information and interprets institutional, core, and major requirements. This position will play a vital role in maximizing student retention by building relationships with students. There are five open Academic Advisor positions. Two in The Peter J. Tobin College of Business, Two in The Lesley H. and William L. Collins College of Professional Studies and one in The Center for Student Success. Only one application is needed. You may indicate in your cover letter if you have a preference of specialty. Job Responsibilities Academic Advising: 70% Provides academic advising for students grounded in tenets of practice outlined by the National Association of Academic Advising (NACADA) and appropriate academic advising and student development theories. Advises for course selection, registration, academic planning, career and educational goal setting, appropriate resources, transitioning to the university, and retention issues. Document student advising outcomes adequately to meet department and institutional disclosure guidelines and aid in subsequent advising activities. Advises in both group and individual settings with current students. Perform appointment preparations including, but not limited to, reviewing all accessible academic records for accuracy and appropriateness of course work, communicating with academic departments for major-specific transfer equivalencies, and requesting the posting of approved transfer courses. Process academic forms and follow-up on processed forms to ensure that the student's record accurately represents the student's chosen major, minor, concentration, and catalog year. Interprets university and college policies and procedures. May be required to work beyond normal office hours including evening and/or on weekends. Student Success & Retention: 20% Advocate for student needs associated with their educational and academic program. Clearly communicate accurate and timely information to students and interpret institutional, general education, and major requirements per the university catalog. Exhibit strong, active listening skills. Help students develop a realistic self-perception and successful transition into the university and help them to establish realistic goals for future endeavors. Monitors academic progress and implements intervention strategies for students who receive academic alerts or who need assistance in maintaining or improving their academic standing. Direct students to resources, programs, and services on campus when it is appropriate to do so. Help students integrate information so that they may make well-informed academic decisions. Work to establish a partnership with students that will guide them efficiently through their academic program. Monitor students advising requirements: Notify students of academic and faculty advising requirements when certain conditions have or have not been met. Maintain accurate and complete student file documentation. Prepare for, present, and advise at first-year student orientations. Support retention efforts include using the Salesforce CRM. Maintain a professional and cordial liaison with administrators, faculty, staff, students, and other involved constituents concerning advisees and program. Additional Duties:10% Complies with all university policies, regulations, rules, procedures, guidelines, and directives in timely manner and adhere to confidentiality policies (FERPA). May provide reports and data analysis of advising initiatives and special populations. Perform other duties as assigned. Competencies, Education, Experience Student-centered advising and commitment to student success Strong verbal and written communication skills Ability to build collaborative, supportive relationships with students and colleagues Critical thinking and problem-solving skills Knowledge of academic policies, degree requirements, and curriculum structures Proficiency with advising technologies and student information systems Cultural competence and commitment to supporting a diverse student population Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Professional judgment, integrity, and adherence to FERPA standards Ability to empower students through guidance, advocacy, and resource referral Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution 1–3 years of experience in academic advising, student affairs, higher education, counseling, or a related field Strong interpersonal and communication skills Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a diverse student population Ability to interpret and apply academic policies, degree requirements, and institutional guidelines Proficiency with student information systems, advising software, and standard office applications (e.g., Microsoft 365) Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage a high-volume caseload Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to FERPA regulations Demonstrated problem-solving skills and the ability to make sound, objective decisions PreferredQualifications Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Student Personnel, or a related field 2–5 years of progressive experience in academic advising or student success roles Experience working in a college or university setting, particularly with developmental or intrusive advising models Familiarity with degree audit systems, retention platforms, and CRM tools (e.g., Banner, Slate, Navigate, Starfish, EAB) Experience working with first-generation, transfer, international, or academically at-risk students Training or certification in academic coaching, student development theory, or counseling techniques Supplemental Information Work Environment: This position operates in a professional office environment within a college or university setting. The role involves frequent interaction with students, faculty, and staff, requiring regular communication via email, phone, video conferencing, and in-person meetings. The employee routinely uses standard office equipment, including computers, phones, photocopiers, and digital advising platforms. The role may require occasional work outside of standard business hours during peak advising periods, such as registration or orientation. Physical Demands: Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Occasional lifting of files, boxes, or office supplies (up to 15 pounds). Manual dexterity required for keyboarding and document handling. Environmental Conditions: This role is typically performed in a climate-controlled office environment with moderate noise levels. Occasional travel between campus buildings or to external locations for meetings, orientations, or events may be required. The workplace environment is fast-paced during peak advising cycles, requiring flexibility and the ability to manage increased workloads. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: This is a full-time position. Standard work hours are Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Longer hours may be required to meet deadlines, as necessary. Travel: Limited, local travel. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5496034/assistant-director-career-advising": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Career Advising",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Career Advising Salary $66,300.00 - $71,100.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600081 Org University Career Services Opening Date 09/25/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s University Career Services is seeking two Assistant Directors for Career Advising to support career readiness and student success. The St. John’s University Career Services team strives to ensure equitable access to career resources for all students as they work towards meaningful and satisfying careers. The ideal candidate will contribute to the growth and sustainability of a comprehensive campus career ecosystem by developing innovative career education content and identifying opportunities for integration across the institution. This individual will deliver high-quality career education programming, provide one-on-one and group career advising, and facilitate meaningful career connections. They will cultivate productive partnerships with faculty to ensure career education is accessible, relevant, and embedded throughout the student experience. Leveraging technology, on-demand resources, outcomes data, and labor market insights, the candidate will provide timely, data-informed career guidance that empowers students to explore opportunities, make informed decisions, navigate career pathways, and achieve their professional goals. The candidate will be part of a centralized team of career professionals, serving both undergraduate and graduate students, and a small population of recent alumni. The Advisor will support the overall effectiveness of the Career Services Department and the Division of Student Affairs. This full-time opportunity offers potential for partial remote work after an initial orientation period. Typically, in the office 4-5 days per week during the semester with increased flexibility on breaks and during the summer. Job Responsibilities • Acquire and maintain comprehensive knowledge of assigned academic programs and pedagogy to provide intentional career programming, resources, and advisement to selected populations. • Collaborate closely with college faculty, departments, student groups, and alumni to develop and lead both foundational training and customized career-related programs. • Maximize access to career resources for all students across St. John’s University’s colleges and campuses, as a member of the centralized University Career Services team. • Provide individual and group advisement to target population(s) while exploring avenues for virtual and on-demand engagement. • Facilitate advanced level career development programming for graduate level students and other targeted groups. • Contribute to the selection and/or development of innovative career planning and job search resources designed to enhance students’ preparedness for post graduate success including the use of AI in the recruitment and job search process. • Remain informed of national, state, and local hiring practices, guidelines, and labor related issues. • Assist students to navigate the career decision making process through activities, programs, and the utilization of career assessment tools when appropriate. • Foster a productive and inclusive environment that encourages student enrollment, retention, persistence, and positive outcomes. • Support the mission and strategic priorities of the University. Competencies, Education, Experience • Bachelor’s Degree required. • Minimum of three to five years of experience in career services, human resources, career coaching, corporate recruiting/business development, or related field. Proven success in developing and maintaining internal and external relationships. • Excellent resume, interviewing and job search skills required. • Must be collaborative, self-directed, outcome oriented, and able to manage multiple projects with shifting priorities. • Possess strong customer service focus for internal and external constituents and success working both independently and in cross-functional teams. • Demonstrate innovative approaches that empower students to successfully navigate the journey from college to career. • Must have familiarity with labor market and industry trends. • Proficient in the use of web-based software, MS Word, PowerPoint and Excel required. • Strong oral and written communication skills; experience teaching, training, or facilitating workshops. Ability to develop and deliver effective presentations to groups. • Some local travel and evening/weekend work required. Preferred qualifications include: • Master’s degree • Familiarity with higher education • Experience with on-campus recruitment • Knowledge of social media as a recruitment and networking tool • Proficiency with Handshake, Virtual Interview Platforms and AI • Familiarity with faith-based organizations *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5502090/administration-economics-adjunct-professor": {
      "title": "Administration & Economics Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Administration & Economics Adjunct Professor Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600082 Org Administration and Economics Opening Date 10/01/2026 Description Benefits Questions St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division/Department Information The Division of Administration & Economics houses the B.S. in Fashion Studies, Program the B.S. in Enterprise Regulation: Profit and Non-Profit, and the A.S. Program in Business Administration. The Fashion Studies Program provides students with knowledge, skills, and experiences to succeed in the industry. The program provides a comprehensive, in-depth, and global approach to studying the business aspects of the fashion industry. The core curriculum consists of courses in various areas of fashion, business, ethics, and sustainability. Foundational knowledge and skills in fashion studies are supported. The Enterprise Regulation: The Profit and Non-Profit program focus on the business industry’s fundamental competencies, which are vital for the field’s future managers. The core curriculum in the liberal arts will provide students with the broad knowledge and strong communication skills that today’s employers expect of well-educated professionals. Business Law knowledge will facilitate effective managers and facilitate effective managers while also cultivating creativity, leadership skills and entrepreneurial abilities that are in wide demand in the business arena. This program provides students with business law knowledge, skills, and experiences to succeed in the business industry. Internships are an integral part of our programs. Internships may be completed in New York and at one of the University’s global campuses, locations in Rome, Paris, and Limerick, Ireland. The St. John’s Community provides internship guidance, mentoring students and provides students with the tutelage to succeed in their chosen career. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities Accounting The adjunct will cover financial accounting concepts that form the basis of external and internal reporting by business entities. They will explain how financial information is communicated to management, stockholders, creditors, and others interested in the status of the business enterprise. The adjunct will cover such topics as the basic accounting framework and concepts: reporting of income, financial position, and cash flows, the accounting process including accruals, and financial statement of elements. Economics We are seeking a passionate and knowledgeable Economics adjunct to teach an introduction to the fundamentals of the economic system. The “macro-economic” approach to employment, prices and economic stability in the context of globalization. The Economics adjunct should be able to also cover the fundamental tools of microeconomics (individual decision-making, markets). The goal is to provide students with a fundamental understanding of economics thinking, enabling them to apply economic concepts to real-world scenarios. Management & Marketing The adjunct instructs students on business principles, marketing research, advertising and strategic management, preparing students for industry careers. The adjunct will introduce problems and processes of management. Emphasis is placed on the principles and practices of management and the functions of the executive. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications All applicants must hold a master’s degree; industry experience is needed. Supplemental Information Application Process Applicants need to submit their CV which needs to include their teaching experience and courses taught and their industry experience to the St. John’s University website at St John's adjunct faculty career page . Contact Dr. Almerinda Forte, Chair, fortea@stjohns.edu for questions regarding the position. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have a Master's degree? Yes No Required Question Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5507457/adjunct-faculty-positions-division-of-sport-management": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Positions - Division of Sport Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Positions - Division of Sport Management Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600087 Org Collins CPS Opening Date 10/06/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division Information The Division of Sport Management seeks adjunct faculty candidates to teach a variety of courses face-to-face (no online, virtual or remote teaching opportunities at this time) in our undergraduate and graduate programs. Rank and salary are based on education level, the quality and quantity of relevant industry experience, and the quality and quantity of college teaching experience. The Division of Sport Management delivers both undergraduate and graduate coursework in areas such as sport management, sport business, sport coaching, international sports, innovation in sports, and interdisciplinary topics such as esports. For more information about the undergraduate program and curriculum, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/spm For more information about the graduate program and curriculum, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/spg Job Responsibilities Responsibilities Adjunct faculty work under the direct supervision of the Division Chair. Once assigned a course or courses, they are expected to: Prepare and distribute to students a course outline in accordance with the course syllabus. Develop instructional materials (lectures, readings, assignments, exams, projects, etc.) that will achieve the learning outcomes as stated in the course syllabus. Evaluate student performance throughout the semester and provide periodic and constructive feedback to students in a reasonable timeframe. Be available to engage with students outside the classroom by email, phone, web conferencing, or face-to-face meetings. Evaluate student performance and post final grades for each student within the timeframe required by the Provost’s Office and be available for two weeks after the semester concludes to discuss final grades with students by email or phone. Promptly respond to requests for information before, during, and after the course as required by the Division Chair and the CCPS Dean’s Office. Competencies, Education, Experience Responsibilities Adjunct faculty work under the direct supervision of the Division Chair. Once assigned a course or courses, they are expected to: Prepare and distribute to students a course outline in accordance with the course syllabus. Develop instructional materials (lectures, readings, assignments, exams, projects, etc.) that will achieve the learning outcomes as stated in the course syllabus. Evaluate student performance throughout the semester and provide periodic and constructive feedback to students in a reasonable timeframe. Be available to engage with students outside the classroom by email, phone, web conferencing, or face-to-face meetings. Evaluate student performance and post final grades for each student within the timeframe required by the Provost’s Office and be available for two weeks after the semester concludes to discuss final grades with students by email or phone. Promptly respond to requests for information before, during, and after the course as required by the Division Chair and the CCPS Dean’s Office. Supplemental Information Application Process Please submit your CV/resume, a document listing teaching experience and courses taught, and a letter of interest online. If and when teaching opportunities arise for which you are qualified, the Chairperson will reach out to you to schedule an interview. If you are selected for a position, additional documentation, such as reference letters and work authorization forms, will be required. Please do not call the Division Chair, Secretary, or the CCPS Deans Office regarding adjunct faculty hiring. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, for the 2026-27 academic year, the minimum per 1-credit* rate is: Adjunct Instructor: $1,803 Adjunct Assistant Professor: $1,906 Adjunct Associate Professor: $2,009 Adjunct Professor: $2,215 *Note: Most classes in the Division of Sport Management are 3-credit classes. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5518473/adjunct-assistant-professor-instructor-in-criminal-justice-or-homeland-security": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor/Instructor in Criminal Justice or Homeland Security",
      "description": "Adjunct Assistant Professor/Instructor in Criminal Justice or Homeland Security Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600095 Org Criminal Justice Homeland Security Opening Date 10/15/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division/Department Information The Criminal Justice and Homeland Security Programs of the Division of Criminal Justice and Homeland Security at St. John’s University invites applications for adjunct positions to teach a variety of different courses for the Spring 2026 semester. The Department is located on the St. John’s University’s Queens campus. The mission of the program is to prepare students for a dynamic career in the criminal justice system and homeland security enterprise with featuring specialized courses, and practical internships to equip graduates for success in both the public and private sectors. For more information about the undergraduate programs, please visit the following pages: Bachelors of Science in Criminal Justice , Bachelors of Science in Homeland Security , and Homeland Security and Criminal Justice Leadership, Master of Professional Studies . For these positions, the division seeks adjunct associate professor/assistant professors/instructors to teach in a face-to-face setting for 85-minute class sessions that meet twice a week in our undergraduate programs. In addition, the division seeks adjunct associate professor/assistant professors/instructors with terminal degrees and online teaching experience to teach in our graduate programs. Rank and salary are based on education level, the quality and quantity of relevant industry experience, and the quality and quantity of college teaching experience. The Division of Criminal Justice and Homeland Security embraces a dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion as the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution. As noted in our Vision Statement, our graduates will excel in the competencies and values required for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities The adjunct faculty member will work under the direct supervision of the Division Chair and will: Prepare and distribute to students a course outline in accordance with the course syllabus. Develop instructional materials (lectures, readings, assignments, exams, projects, etc.) that will achieve the learning outcomes as stated in the course syllabus. Evaluate student performance throughout the semester and provide periodic and constructive feedback to students. Evaluate student performance and post grades for each student as directed by the Provost’s Office and offer availability to discuss grades with students in person, by email or phone. Promptly respond to requests for information before, during, and after the course as required by the Division Chair and the CCPS Dean’s Office. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications Teaching and experience are at the core of being an effective adjunct faculty member, so experience both in teaching in higher education in the field of law enforcement, corrections, emergency management, intelligence, investigations, critical infrastructure protection, and security related fields. Minimum requirements for teaching in the undergraduate programs include a master's degree and a minimum of five years of significant work experience in the field. Minimum requirements for teaching in the graduate programs include a terminal degree, a minimum of five years of significant work experience in the field, and previous online teaching experience Supplemental Information Application Process Applicants need to submit their CV which needs to include their teaching experience and courses taught and their industry experience to the St. John’s University website at the adjunct faculty career page. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position $1,803 per contact hour for an Adjunct Instructor, $1,906 per contact hour for an Adjunct Assistant Professor, and $2,009 per contact hour for an Adjunct Associate Professor. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5384805/associate-director-of-recruitment-marketing-and-partnerships-gsrm": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Recruitment, Marketing, and Partnerships (GSRM)",
      "description": "Associate Director of Recruitment, Marketing, and Partnerships (GSRM) Salary $83,600.00 - $94,050.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600023 Org Greenberg School of Risk Management Opening Date 09/24/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Reporting to the Executive Director of Admission and Recruitment, Associate Director of Recruitment, Marketing, and Partnerships (GSRM) for the Maurice R. Greenberg School of Risk Management and Insurance plays a pivotal role in advancing the visibility, enrollment, and industry engagement efforts of GSRM. This position leads strategic initiatives to promote Greenberg's undergraduate and graduate programs, strengthen relationships with corporate and professional partners, and attract a highly qualified and diverse pool of students. The Associate Director will be a strategic thinker and creative marketer with strong relationship management skills and a deep understanding of risk management, insurance, and actuarial science industries. This is a three-year, term-limited position funded by endowed resources. Continuation beyond the initial term is contingent upon funding and performance following a review approximately 2.5 years into the appointment. Job Responsibilities Marketing & Brand Development Develop, implement, and assess an integrated marketing and communication plan for GSRM's academic programs, events, and initiatives. Partner with the University's Marketing and Communications team to align GSRM branding with institutional standards while highlighting its distinctive industry reputation. Create content for digital, print, and social media platforms that tell GSRM's story and showcases student success, faculty expertise, and industry connections. Track and analyze marketing metrics to inform future strategies and ensure measurable results. Oversee the production of recruitment materials, event collateral, and digital campaigns tailored to GSRM's audiences (prospective students, employers, alumni, and industry partners). Recruitment & Enrollment Management Serve as the liaison to Undergraduate and Graduate Admission for all GSRM-reIated recruitment and enrollment efforts. Design and execute recruitment strategies to increase applications, yield, and diversity among undergraduate and graduate students. Represent GSRM at recruitment events, information sessions, professional conferences, and industry networking opportunities. Cultivate relationships with high schools, universities, and professional organizations that serve as pipelines for GSRM programs. Provide program-specific presentations, webinars, and one-on-one consultations to prospective students and their families. Collaborate with academic advisors, faculty, and alumni to support admitted student conversion and enrollment goals. Partnership & Industry Engagement Strengthen existing corporate and organizational partnerships and establish new ones that enhance experiential learning, internships, scholarships, and employment opportunities for students. Work closely with the GSRM Board of Overseers, alumni network, and industry leaders to identify strategic collaborations that elevate the school's profile and impact. Coordinate GSRM-sponsored events, such as executive panels, networking receptions, and industry conferences, to increase engagement and visibility. Support employer relations initiatives in collaboration with the University Career Services team. Strategic Planning & Reporting Develop and manage annual goals, budgets, and timelines for marketing, recruitment, and partnership initiatives. Provide regular reports on recruitment outcomes, partnership engagement, and marketing performance to the Executive Director and senior leadership. Stay informed on trends in risk management, insurance, and higher education recruitment to ensure GSRM remains competitive and innovative. Competencies, Education, Experience A Bachelor's degree required; a Master's degree in Marketing, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field is preferred. Experience in higher education is preferred; 5—7 years of relevant experience in admission, enrollment, management, or higher education marketing. Progressively responsible experience in marketing, recruitment, or partnership development, ideally within higher education or the insurance/risk management industry. Excellent analytical, communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills with the ability to engage diverse audiences. Proven success in developing and executing marketing campaigns and strategic recruitment initiatives. Experience managing corporate and institutional partnerships. Demonstrated ability to think strategically, manage multiple projects simultaneously, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency with CRM systems (Slate preferred), digital marketing tools, and data analytics platforms. Flexibility to work evenings, mornings, and weekends. A valid driver's license. Required Education and Experience: A Bachelor's degree or equivalent is required. Minimum of 5-7 years relevant experience with progressive leadership responsibilities is required. Relevant admission and recruitment experience is required. Excellent analytical, communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills required. Understanding of discretion related to handling confidential information is required. Flexibility to work occasion evening and weekends is required. Preferred Education and Experience: Master's degree is preferred. Relevant experience or knowledge of the insurance industry is preferred. Ability to multi-task and manage multiple priorities with short notice and changing deadlines is preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications A valid driver's license is required. Flexibility to work early mornings, evenings, and weekends for recruitment events is required. Supplemental Information Work Environment This job operates in a professional office environment and routinely uses standard office equipment such as personal computers, printers, etc. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand for a few hours at recruitment events ; move about; sit; to carry work and use controls; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; communicate. The employee must occasionally lift or move up to 251bs of recruitment materials. Specific vision abilities required by the employee include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and the ability to adjust focus. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Thursday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. and Friday 8:30am-3:OOpm. Early morning, night, and weekend hours are required for recruitment events. Travel Travel for recruitment events and periodic travel to branch campuses, including the Manhattan campus, is required. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5435209/assistant-professor-business-analytics-and-information-systems-peter-j-tobin-co": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business) Salary $95,000.00 - $115,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Contract Faculty Job Number 202600032 Org Peter J Tobin College of Business Opening Date 08/04/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Institution St. John’s University, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs across its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of online offerings. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. The College Originally founded in 1927, the AACSB-accredited Peter J. Tobin College of Business now has more than 3,000 students in a wide variety of undergraduate and graduate programs, all supported by more than 150 faculty, administrators, and staff on the Queens and Manhattan, NY, campuses. The Tobin College’s highly ranked programs are led by an outstanding faculty of teacher-scholars, widely recognized for their excellent teaching and expertise in various business areas. The Tobin undergraduate business program is ranked #50 by Poets & Quants, and our Online MBA program is ranked #42 by U.S. News & World Report. For more information, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/academics/schools/peter-j-tobin-college-business . The Department The Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems of the Tobin College of Business of St. John’s University is inviting applications for a non-tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level starting in Fall 2026. The Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems is a thriving, driven department with 12 tenure-track/tenured faculty members. The Business Analytics department offers the following degrees: B.S. in Business Analytics, M.S. in Business Analytics, MBA concentration in Information Systems, and MBA concentration in Business Analytics. For more information on the Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/resources/places/business-analytics-information-systems. Commitment to Equal Opportunity St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. It is understood that any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment, and education. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities include maintaining an active research profile, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, and contributing to the university through service, all of which are essential at the Tobin College of Business. The candidate should be able to teach a wide range of business analytics courses, from introductory to advanced levels. Our faculty engage in professional development, program development, assessment, and service to the University and broader community. Candidates should be familiar with technology-supported learning pedagogy and be able to integrate technology, particularly AI, into teaching. Furthermore, candidates should be able to use different teaching modalities, including face-to-face, online, and hybrid. Competencies, Education, Experience A DBA or Ph.D. in Data Science, Statistics, Business Analytics, or a closely related field is required for this position. ABDs in advanced dissertation stages will be considered. A successful applicant should be an effective, empathetic teacher at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and actively participate in different service-related activities. All specialization areas in Business Analytics will be considered; however, particular attention will be given to candidates with expertise in data mining, artificial intelligence, analytical computing, statistics, and decision sciences. Preference will be given to candidates who can support the growth of undergraduate and graduate programs. Supplemental Information Application Process Candidates are invited to apply online. Applicants will need to include an application letter, a resume/CV (including the names and contact information of 3 references), a teaching philosophy, and photocopies or official transcripts. Preference will be given to candidates who can support the growth of undergraduate and graduate programs. The selection process begins July 24, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Link to Apply: Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems Non-Tenure Track TF27-TOB-08 *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
