    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5462213/director-emergency-management-business-continuity": {
      "title": "Director, Emergency Management & Business Continuity",
      "description": "Director, Emergency Management & Business Continuity Salary $126,800.00 - $144,250.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600065 Org Public Safety Opening Date 09/21/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Director of Emergency Management and Continuity at St. John’s University is a subject matter expert in all aspects of emergency management—including planning, prevention, response, and recovery—as well as business and operational continuity. Using an all-hazards approach, the Director identifies and mitigates risks that could potentially disrupt university operations at any of St. John’s locations, domestic or international. With a strong operational focus, the Director ensures that emergency management plans are actionable, widely understood, appropriately resourced, and routinely exercised. The goal is to protect lives, property, and university assets while building a resilient institution capable of operating through and recovering from crises. This position also authors and manages the university’s enterprise continuity program, coordinating across schools, departments, and global locations. The Director ensures all continuity plans remain current and effective in supporting St. John’s through both expected and unexpected disruptions. This role plays a vital part in ensuring university governance, operations, and recovery can continue in the face of man-made or natural incidents. An effective communicator, strategic thinker, and skilled project manager, the Director is responsive in emergencies, anticipates risk, closes capability gaps, and fosters a culture of preparedness. This position also collaborates closely with the University’s Operations to develop and execute Homeland Security Exercise and Evaluation Program (HSEEP)-compliant exercises. The role carries 24/7 emergency responsibilities. Job Responsibilities Policies, Plans, and Procedures – 40% Lead stakeholder committees to develop and maintain emergency and continuity plans. Conduct multi-disciplinary risk assessments and hazard mitigation planning. Create, maintain and update the university-wide Comprehensive Emergency Management Plan (CEMP). Tailor Emergency Operations Plans (EOPs) for each campus or center, including international locations. Ensure compliance with regulatory and accessibility standards. Collaborate with departments and schools to maintain continuity plans that prioritize core missions (teaching, research, housing, and public service). Coordinate with Enterprise Risk Management and international campus leaders. Establish and maintain a University-wide travel security governance framework that sets institutional standards for University-sponsored travel risk management, including decision authority, risk-tolerance thresholds by destination, and approval and documentation expectations applicable to faculty, staff, and students. Oversee an operational travel security program that provides a single intake and tracking mechanism forUniversity-sponsored travel, conducts trip-level risk reviews, delivers pre-departure briefings for elevated-risk locations, and coordinates active traveler communications and emergency response. Establish a mandatory travel insurance standard covering emergency medical treatment, medical evacuation, trip disruption, and repatriation; enforce verification as part of the travel registration workflow. Exercises and Outreach – 20% Design and deliver HSEEP-compliant training, exercises, and public preparedness campaigns. Maintain a multi-year training and exercise calendar. Develop outreach programs for students, faculty, and staff on preparedness and resilience. Build partnerships with NYC Emergency Management, regional universities, and professional associations. Community Education and Engagement – 15% Develop and lead campus-wide education and outreach initiatives to promote understanding of emergency management tools, plans, and individual preparedness responsibilities. Deliver engaging, accessible content to students, faculty, and staff through workshops, briefings, printed materials, digital campaigns, and orientation programs. Ensure emergency plans and continuity tools are not only developed but also understood and embraced by the campus community. Partner with Student Affairs, Residence Life, Human Resources, and academic units to embed preparedness education into community life and institutional culture. Foster a culture of shared responsibility and proactive risk reduction. Strategy and Continuous Improvement – 15% Serve as a standards champion across departments to build institutional resilience. Identify and prioritize innovative risk reduction strategies. Track corrective actions and incorporate lessons learned from exercises and incidents. Advance the integration of continuity into emergency response planning. Implement a travel risk intelligence and monitoring capability with centralized visibility into active University-sponsored trips, automated country/city risk ratings, alerts for emerging global incidents, and direct support for emergency response coordination, with redundant access for Public Safety and program administrators. Emergency Response – 5% Serve as Incident Commander orassistin ICS role assignment during EOC activations. Lead operational setup and readiness for all potential EOC sites. Deploy to incident locations as needed and support international response operations. Partnership Development – 5% Establish partnerships with peer institutions andprivate-sectorstakeholders. Facilitate integration, liaison, and best-practice sharing across continuity communities. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Education: Bachelor’s degree in Emergency Management, Public Administration, Business, or related field. Required Experience: Minimum of 7 years of emergency management/continuity or program management experience; or 5–7 years with a related graduate degree. Minimum of 5 years in a supervisory capacity. Required Skills and Certifications: Demonstrated expertise in crisis and continuity planning. Familiarity with FEMA, NIMS, HSEEP, and regulatory frameworks. Familiarity with travel risk management frameworks, including country/destination risk ratings, traveler tracking platforms, pre-departure briefings, and institutional duty-of-care obligations. Completion of ICS courses: IS 100, IS 200, IS 700, IS 800. Valid driver’s license (or ability to obtain a NY license). Strong communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple projects in a fast-paced, high-stakesenvironment. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree (MBA or related field). Certified Emergency Manager (CEM), CBCP, or FEMA MEP certification. Experience in a higher education or global enterprise setting . Strong data management and information security awareness. Supplemental Information Institutional Impact The Director strengthens university-wide resilience and governance during emergencies. Leads major event planning support and contributes to unplanned incident response. Manages a significant Public Safety budget and partners with all university departments. Authority and Decision-Making Develops and advises on emergency and continuity policies. Makes real-time decisions during crises, including priority-setting and resource deployment. Advisessenior university leadership on readiness, response, and recovery strategies. Key Relationships Collaborates with university leaders, Public Safety personnel, faculty, and operations teams. Serves asliaisonto external emergency agencies and peer institutions. RepresentsPublic Safety in university-wide meetings on risk, continuity, and compliance. Direct Reports One Manager (to be hired) *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5490447/associate-provost-strategic-planning-academic-budget-planning": {
      "title": "Associate Provost Strategic Planning & Academic Budget Planning",
      "description": "Associate Provost Strategic Planning & Academic Budget Planning Salary $173,600.00 - $197,500.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600078 Org Office of the Provost Opening Date 09/22/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Associate Provost for Strategic Planning and Academic Budget Planning serves as the senior operational leader for the academic budget planning division within OASPA and the primary deputy to the Vice Provost for academic budget planning. This position is accountable for the performance, consistency, quality, and strategic direction of academic budget planning across all assigned academic portfolios. The Associate Provost sets division-wide planning standards, supervises Assistant Provosts, reviews portfolio-level recommendations, resolves cross-portfolio issues, and ensures that academic budget planning is integrated with assessment, accreditation, grants, faculty planning, enrollment-informed analysis, program review, and strategic resource allocation. This role may also manage the most complex academic portfolios directly, as assigned, and acts on behalf of the Vice Provost in institutional planning discussions when delegated. The Associate Provost ensures that school-level budget plans reflect institutional strategy, financial discipline, academic priorities, and long-term sustainability. Job Responsibilities Division Leadership and Strategic Direction · Set the strategic direction, standards, timelines, and expectations for academic budget planning across the division. · Translate Vice Provost priorities into operating direction for Assistant Provosts and portfolio teams. · Ensure consistency, analytical rigor, and strategic alignment across academic budget planning portfolios. · Monitor cross-portfolio financial trends, risks, structural issues, and resource opportunities. · Resolve escalated portfolio issues and determine which matters require Vice Provost review. · Serve as the primary academic budget planning liaison to the Associate Provosts for Academic Assessment and Accreditation and Grants and Sponsored Research. Assistant Provost Supervision and Development · Supervise, mentor, and evaluate Assistant Provosts responsible for assigned school and college portfolios. · Review significant portfolio recommendations, budget decisions, and financial analyses before escalation or presentation to senior leadership. · Build Assistant Provost capacity for independent judgment, Dean-level advising, and increasingly complex portfolio leadership. · Lead cross-portfolio training and knowledge development to ensure consistency, continuity, and institutional fluency across the team. Direct Portfolio Management · Manage budget planning for assigned complex portfolios, including annual budget development, multi-year financial projections, position planning, salary planning, and strategic resource analysis. · Serve as the primary financial planning partner to assigned Deans for complex or high-risk portfolios. · Conduct program-level financial analyses, P&L/ROI assessments, pro forma modeling, and scenario analyses. · Identify risks, structural deficits, staffing concerns, enrollment exposure, and resource opportunities requiring Vice Provost or Provost-level attention. Integrated Planning · Ensure budget plans incorporate relevant assessment findings, accreditation requirements, grant activity, faculty capacity, restricted fund availability, and strategic priorities. · Set standards for how assessment, accreditation, and grants-related information should inform financial planning. · Oversee financial dimensions of accreditation, grant-funded commitments, cost-share planning, and program review across portfolios. · Ensure academic budget planning supports institutional accountability, financial sustainability, and academic quality. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Qualifications · Master’s degree or equivalent work experience. · Minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible experience in academic budget planning, institutional finance, academic administration, or related higher education work. · At least 5 years of experience in a senior leadership, supervisory, or portfolio management role. · Demonstrated expertise in academic budget planning, multi-year modeling, faculty workforce planning, salary planning, resource allocation, and program financial analysis. · Experience advising Provosts, Vice Provosts, Deans, or senior academic leaders. · Demonstrated ability to lead professional staff, exercise independent judgment, and manage complex financial decisions. · Strong executive communication, analytical, strategic planning, and relationship-building skills. Preferred Qualifications · Doctoral degree in a relevant field. · Experience in a Provost’s Office, Academic Affairs, or central university planning environment. · Experience with Banner, Argos, Weave, FLAC, and academic financial reporting systems. · Experience integrating budget planning with assessment, accreditation, grants, and program review. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5493124/computer-science-mathematics-and-science-adjunct-professor": {
      "title": "Computer Science, Mathematics and Science Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Computer Science, Mathematics and Science Adjunct Professor Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600079 Org Computer Science, Math, and Science Opening Date 09/23/2026 Description Benefits Questions St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division/Department Information The Division of Computer Science, Mathematics and Science delivers undergraduate programs in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology all ABET accredited as well as an undergraduate degree in Healthcare Informatics. Additionally, it offers ABET accredited graduate programs in AI and Data Science and Cyber and Information Security as well as a graduate program in Computer Science. For more information about the Division, please visit https://www.stjohns.edu/resources/places/computer-science-mathematics-and-science Job Responsibilities Responsibilities The division is seeking candidates for all ranks at the adjunct level to teach computer science, cybersecurity, networking systems, information technology or mathematicscourses. Adjunct faculty work under the direct supervision of the Division Chair. Once assigned a course or courses, they are expected to: · Prepare and distribute to students a course outline in accordance with the course syllabus. · Develop instructional materials (lectures, readings, assignments, exams, projects, etc.) that will achieve the learning outcomes as stated in the course syllabus. · Evaluate student performance throughout the semester and provide periodic and constructive feedback to students in a reasonable amount of time. · Be available to engage with students outside the classroom by email, phone, web conferencing, or face-to-face meetings. · Evaluate student performance and post final grades for each student within the timeframe required by the Provost’s Office and be available for two weeks after the semester concludes to discuss final grades with students by email or phone. · Promptly respond to requests for information before, during, and after the course as required by the Division Chair and the CCPS Dean’s Office. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications For all ranks, a master’s degree in the discipline or a related field is required. At the instructor level, relevant industry experience and college teaching experience is preferred. At the assistant professor level, college teaching experience is required. At the associate professor level, college teaching experience is required, and an earned doctorate in a related field is preferred. At the full professor level, extensive college teaching experience, and an earned doctorate in a related field isrequired. Supplemental Information Application Process For all ranks, a master’s degree in the discipline or a related field is required. At the instructor level, relevant industry experience and college teaching experience is preferred. At the assistant professor level, college teaching experience is required. At the associate professor level, college teaching experience is required, and an earned doctorate in a related field is preferred. At the full professor level, extensive college teaching experience, and an earned doctorate in a related field isrequired. Applicants need to submit their CV which needs to include their teaching experience and courses taught and their industry experience to the St. John’s University website at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns?jobType%5b0%5d=Contract%20Faculty&jobType%5b1%5d=Full-Time%20Faculty&jobType%5b2%5d=Part-Time%20Faculty&sort=PositionTitle%7CAscending In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is Adjunct Instructor $1,803 per contact hour, Adjunct Assistant $1,906 per contact hour, Adjunct Associate $2,009 per contact hour, and Adjunct Professor $2,215 per contact hour. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have a master's degree? Yes No Required Question Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5519473/events-supervisor": {
      "title": "Events Supervisor",
      "description": "Events Supervisor Salary $72,700.00 - $81,800.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600097 Org Public Safety Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Events Supervisor is responsible for supervising internal and external University events. A critical function of the Public Safety Event Supervisor is his/her attendance at meetings with the planning members of the Athletics Department, Student life (Greek Life), Conference Services and Public Safety. The Events Supervisor is responsible for reviewing and evaluating the nine thousand passes generated yearly for both internal and external events here on campus. The Events Supervisor must evaluate how many Public Safety Officers are required to keep each event as safe as humanly possible while maintaining a balance within the University’s budget constraints. Job Responsibilities Supervise the events on campus to include both internal University events and outside events. This will include preparing the roll calls for the events and assigning the personnel scheduled to work that event. • Schedule and call the Per Diems for events, patrol, shuttle and Resident Village coverage. • Supervise and monitor the Per Diems for uniforms, appearance, customer service skills and communication skills. When necessary prepare disciplinary records for problematic Per Diems. • Notify the Assistant Director, Administration & Events by email on all payroll changes, disciplinary problems and all other pertinent information. • After every event email the Director, Public Safety and Assistant Director, Administration & Events with a critique of the event including any problems or issues, attendance, name of the event and all other pertinent information. • During events where any problems or issues necessitate making notifications to an outside agency or other administrators within the University, notify Chief of Public Safety and Director, Public Safety immediately by cell phone. • Backfill for the Supervisors assigned to steady tour when they are on vacation and in emergency situations. Backfill for Supervisors when no events are scheduled to cover. • Monitor all campus calendars to make sure they are up to date on events and activities. Make sure the Per Diem Officers are continually instructed at roll calls before the events begin. Also make sure that the Per Diems are communicating the correct information to the University community. • Supervise all department reports prepared by the Per Diems for accuracy. Make sure the Per Diems are instructed on accuracy and neatness. If Per Diems require special instruction to assure that the reports are accurate and completed correctly, provide them with the necessary time. • Continously reaffirm the policy and procedures of the department; make sure the Per Diems are updated and instructed. • Continually assess customer service via dialogue with Public Safety personnel and feedback from the community Competencies, Education, Experience • Bachelor’s degree preferred • 5-10 years of experience in security and/or Police environment preferred. • Proficiency with MS Word, Excel, Outlook, Banner, UIS • Excellent customer service skills are required • Ability to multitask • Attention to detail • Excellent verbal and written communication skills • Ability to exercise high level of discretion, good judgment, and professionalism • Capacity to work in a fast-paced, unpredictable environment • Must be highly flexible and accessible after normal business hours. Schedule will be pre\u0002approved by Assistant Director, Administration & Events. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5436850/financial-aid-advisor-federal-programs": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs)",
      "description": "Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs) Salary $66,300.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600035 Org Financial Aid Opening Date 09/21/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Financial Aid Advisor plays a critical role in advancing the University’s commitment to Student Success by ensuring access to financial resources, providing personalized guidance, and collaborating across departments to remove financial barriers that may impact retention and graduation. Under the general direction and reporting to the Sr. Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, the Advisor will assist in the management of key federal aid processes, including the, Federal Pell Grant program, TEACH Grant program and federal verification, while delivering exceptional service to a diverse student population. Job Responsibilities Federal Aid Administration and Compliance Collaborate with the Senior Assistant Director and Senior Associate Director to ensure the federal financial aid process is seamless and student - centered. Maintain a working knowledge of federal and state financial aid regulations and University policies. Monitor document management workflows to ensure compliance with federal requirements. Assist with the timely processing, reconciliation, and reporting of the Federal Pell Grant program. Manage the federal TEACH Grant program, including reconciliation and required reporting. Support administration of the University’s Course Program of Study (CPOS) process and related aid impacts. Verification and Aid Packaging Review and complete federal verification cases for new first - year students, ensuring accuracy and regulatory compliance. Package financial aid for transfer students admitted for the spring semester. Exercise strong attention to detail and accountability when reviewing documentation and determining aid eligibility. Professional Judgment and Student Advocacy Evaluate and apply Professional Judgment for students with special circumstances in accordance with federal guidelines. Support the equitable delivery of financial aid by accurately assessing individual student financial situations. Counseling, Service, and Student Engagement Provide individualized financial aid counseling to students and families, including guidance on aid programs and verification requirements. Serve as Counselor of the Day and provide backup support for the Student Financial Services Center. Deliver professional, responsive service to students, families, alumni, and external partners. Outreach, Collaboration, and Process Improvement Utilize data to identify opportunities for operational improvement and increased student engagement. Partner with Enrollment and other University departments to support holistic student success. Conduct financial aid presentations, workshops, and virtual sessions on financial aid topics and financial literacy. Represent Student Financial Services at recruitment and onboarding events, including Open House and Accepted Student Day (evenings and weekends required). Additional Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of departmental and institutional goals. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Supervisory Responsibility Assist with managing student workers Other Duties This job description is not exhaustive and may include additional responsibilities as assigned. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Competencies, Education, Experience Ability to learn and apply federal, state regulations and university policies in support of the timely delivery of federal student aid. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Excellent attention to detail, multitasking, and prioritization skills. Ability to manage complex conversations and resolve escalated concerns with empathy and professionalism. Effective communication and presentation skills (in-person and virtual) Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite. Preferred Education and Experience: Experience with Ellucian Banner. Prior experience in higher education Additional Eligibility Qualifications Must be qualified to access Federal Student Aid systems Supplemental Information Work Environment Professional office environment. Role requires routinely uses a computer, standard office equipment such as copiers, phones/voice mail, fax, scanner, printers, etc. This individual is routinely exposed to indoor environment with moderate noise level and on occasion may need to work outside. The job is an on-campus position but must be prepared to work remotely if needed and must have access to Wi-Fi, laptop, and a cell phone. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is routinely required to sit, stand, and move about, to carry work, reach with hands and arms, climb stairs, communicate, and hear. The employee must occasionally lift or move up to 25 lbs. Specific vision abilities required by the employee include close vision, distance vision, color vision, depth perception, the ability to adjust focus and all-day use of a computer. Employee frequently exercises flexibility (ability to shift from one task to another). Employees routinely work within time constraints and maintain attentiveness intensity. Employees are frequently involved in social interactions that require oral and written communication. Employees are required to hear conversations in moderate noise environments. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time, Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Some evening and weekend work required for enrollment events. Travel This is an on-campus position and requires daily travel to campus, occasional travel to other locations for presentations and training. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5439551/financial-aid-advisor-data-research": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor (Data Research)",
      "description": "Financial Aid Advisor (Data Research) Salary $66,300.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600038 Org Financial Aid Opening Date 09/21/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Financial Aid Advisor – Research and Data supports the Office of Student Financial Services by managing financial aid reporting, compliance, and data analysis functions while also providing student counseling. This position reports to the Director for Student Financial Services and is not responsible for direct supervision, but plays a critical role in supporting departmental operations, compliance, and data-driven decision-making. Job Responsibilities Generate and analyze weekly, monthly, and annual financial aid reports related to enrollment, scholarships, and endowments to support institutional planning and monitoring Assist in the preparation and submission of federal and state reports, including IPEDS, HEGIS, and FISAP, ensuring accuracy and compliance Collaborate with the Office of Institutional Data to complete external surveys and reporting requests, including Common Data Set, U.S. News, and Peterson’s Respond to internal and external data requests from university leadership and external agencies Run and maintain weekly audit reports, identifying discrepancies and developing new reports as needed to strengthen internal controls Review and process federal verification cases, ensuring compliance with Title IV regulations through detailed and accurate documentation review Provide financial aid counseling to prospective and enrolled students and families, assisting with financial planning and decision-making Assist with problem resolution related to financial aid eligibility, processing, and student accounts Deliver high-quality customer service to a diverse population, including students, families, faculty, staff, and external partners Perform other duties as assigned by the Director for Student Financial Services Additional Responsibilities: Perform other duties as assigned in support of departmental and institutional goals. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Technical / Hard Skills : Knowledge of federal and state financial aid regulations (Title IV) Strong data analysis and reporting skills Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and reporting tools Prior experience with student information systems and financial aid systems (e.g., Banner, PeopleSoft, or similar) is preferred Ability to manage multiple reporting deadlines Soft Skills: Strong attention to detail and problem-solving skills Effective communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain complex financial information Ability to provide student-centered service in a fast-paced environment Strong organizational and time management skills Ability to work collaboratively across departments Supervisory Responsibility This position does not require supervisory experience. Other Duties This job description is not exhaustive and may include additional responsibilities as assigned. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree Experience in financial aid, higher education administration, or data reporting Experience with federal financial aid programs and compliance requirements Experience with Microsoft Office Suite Preferred Education and Experience: Master’s degree in higher education administration, business, or related field 3–5 years of progressive experience in financial aid or institutional research Experience with data reports for external agencies (IPEDS, Common Data Set, etc.) Experience with Ellucian Banner Prior experience in higher education Additional Eligibility Qualifications Ability to maintain knowledge of current federal and state regulations Must be qualified to access Federal Student Aid system Supplemental Information Work Environment Professional office environment. Role requires routinely uses a computer, standard office equipment such as copiers, phones/voice mail, fax, scanner, printers, etc. This individual is routinely exposed to indoor environment with moderate noise level and on occasion may need to work outside. The job is an on-campus position but must be prepared to work remotely if needed and must have access to Wi-Fi, laptop, and a cell phone. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is routinely required to sit, stand, and move about, to carry work, reach with hands and arms, climb stairs, communicate, and hear. The employee must occasionally lift or move up to 25 lbs. Specific vision abilities required by the employee include close vision, distance vision, color vision, depth perception, the ability to adjust focus and all-day use of a computer. Employee frequently exercises flexibility (ability to shift from one task to another). Employees routinely work within time constraints and maintain attentiveness intensity. Employees are frequently involved in social interactions that require oral and written communication. Employees are required to hear conversations in moderate noise environments. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time, Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Some evening and weekend work required for enrollment events. Travel This is an on-campus position and requires daily travel to campus, occasional travel to other locations for presentations and training. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5446222/part-time-licensed-mental-health-counselor": {
      "title": "Part-Time Licensed Mental Health Counselor",
      "description": "Part-Time Licensed Mental Health Counselor Salary $57.00 Hourly Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Staff Job Number 202600042 Org Student Wellness Opening Date 09/23/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Title: Part -Time Licensed Mental Health Counselor (Hourly) Department: Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS) Campus: Queens Position Description: St. John’s University seeking a compassionate and qualified Licensed Mental Health Counselor to join the CAPS our team on a part-time, hourly basis . This role is ideal for a dedicated clinician interested in supporting college students’ mental health and wellness through evening and weekend services. The counselor will provide direct clinical services, including individual and group counseling, crisis intervention, consultation, and outreach programming. Services will be offered primarily during evenings and on weekends to best meet student needs. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities: Provide short-term, goal-oriented individual counseling to a diverse student population. Conduct crisis intervention and risk assessments; provide referrals as needed. Maintain timely and accurate clinical documentation in accordance with ethical and legal standards. Collaborate with campus partners (e.g., Student Affairs, Residence Life, Academic Advising) as needed for coordinated student care. Participate in outreach and wellness events that promote mental health awareness. Uphold confidentiality and ethical practices in alignment with professional standards and university policy. Attend required staff meetings and supervision, as scheduled. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher in Counseling, Psychology, Social Work, or a related field. Active and unrestricted licensure in the state (e.g., LMHC, LCSW, LPC, or equivalent). Minimum of 1 year of post-licensure clinical experience, preferably in a college or young adult setting. Strong clinical skills in assessment, crisis response, and brief counseling. Experience working with diverse populations, including BIPOC, LGBTQ+, international students, and students with disabilities. Strong diagnostic and therapeutic skills, particularly using short-term treatment interventions. Demonstrated commitment to the highest ethical standards of professional practice, as well as personal and professional integrity. Ability to work as part of a multi-disciplinary team and to collaborate with other departments and college administrators. Strong crisis assessment and crisis management skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Supplemental Information In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly rate for this position is $57.00 . St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. * Important Note- St. John’s is NOT a n E-Verify Employer Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer . ?All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5450988/math-teacher": {
      "title": "Math Teacher",
      "description": "Math Teacher Salary $50.00 Hourly Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Staff Job Number 202600052 Org Diversity and Inclusivity Opening Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Title: Math Teacher - Part Time Department: Academic Support Services Campus: Queens Program Description: Liberty Partnerships Program The Liberty Partnerships Program is sponsored by the New York State Education Department and St John's University. It is designed to provide support services to high school students who are identified as having the potential to pursue a college education but need assistance to complete secondary school. The program provides a broad range of services designed to increase academic skill development, motivation to succeed, and foster the personal development of the students in the program. These year-round services include: tutoring, counseling, mentoring, developmental courses, and social and enrichment activities. The program consists of a Director, 1 Program Coordinator, 1 part-time Graduate Assistant, and a team of part-time teachers and college tutors/mentors. The Math Teacher is responsible for providing instruction and tutorial services in mathematics during the LPP Saturday and after-school program located at John Adams High School or the SJU campus. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities: Provide instruction in the area of mathematics (pre-algebra, algebra, and geometry) and; Collaborate with High School Liaisons and/or school personnel to design and implement academic interventions for students; Assist in coordinating tutorial services; conducting tutorial training; and supervising tutorial staff; Exhibit great classroom management skills that enable learning for all students; Perform other duties as assigned by the Project Director. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications: Master's Degree in Education; State certification or college teaching experience; Three years of teaching experience at the secondary or collegiate level; Excellent verbal and written communication skills; Knowledge of NYS Learning Standards and Common Core; Ability to inspire and motivate youth; Deep-rooted passion in serving students and helping them achieve their goals; Preference given to an educator who currently serves as a full-time teacher at the target high school. Hours: 6 hours weekly, some evenings or weekends required (some hybrid remote options may be available via Zoom for evening or weekend parent meetings and/or workshops only). Evenings or weekends are substituted when necessary and are not an addition to the regular work schedule-10 hours weekly max. Position Type: Part-Time (Saturdays only, 10:00 am – 1:00 pm). Supplemental Information In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly salary for this position is $50 . St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment, and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer.?All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
