    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5451043/public-safety-officer-dispatcher": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher Salary $25.00 Hourly Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Public Safety Job Number 202600054 Org Public Safety Opening Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Department: Public Safety Specific Job Title: ?Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher Campus:? Queens, Manhattan Command Center Dispatcher is assigned to the Public Safety Command Center and serves as the first point of contact for all emergency and non-emergency calls across the St. John’s University global enterprise. They serve as radio, telephone and computer based dispatchers of assignments, deployment of resources, and other support services (i.e. law enforcement, fire, medical, etc.). They operate and monitor multi-channel radio, security, CCTV, and warning systems for timely detection and response to local and global events and incidents. They also perform other clerical and administrative duties related to the Public Safety Mission. This role will report directly to Public Safety Supervisors. This position supports St. John’s University’s campus safety and is the first point of contact in high-stress situations, playing a critical role in ensuring prompt, professional response to incidents. Job Responsibilities Emergency Communication and Dispatch: Receive, prioritize, and document emergency and non-emergency calls from the St. John’s campus community. Dispatch public safety officers and appropriate first responders using a two-way radio system and computer-aided dispatch software. Monitor and respond to campus fire alarms, intrusion alarms, and access control alerts. Provide exceptional customer service, information, support, and assistance to all University community members including students, staff, faculty, and guests. Additionally , ensuring that all requests for service or information are directed to the relevant person or office as required. Initiate mass notifications through the emergency notification system during certain incidents Monitoring and Surveillance: Continuously monitor campus CCTV systems, access control, and emergency notification systems. Report suspicious activity or safety hazards to appropriate personnel for immediate response. Assist in activating emergency response protocols and campus alerts as needed. Maintain continuous awareness of Department of Public Safety personnel in the field or on special assignments. Information Management and Reporting: Maintain accurate and detailed records of calls, officer activity, incidents, and responses. Assist with the preparation of incident summaries and reports for St. John’s University officials and law enforcement. Perform data entry into public safety records management systems. Campus and Community Support: Provide information and support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors regarding public safety policies, resources, and procedures. Answer questions and route calls to appropriate university departments. Demonstrate empathy, calm, and professionalism in all interactions. Engage with the various campus community departments. Be mindful of current crime trends on and around the campus grounds and take appropriate action to deter such activity. Operational Support: Test and report equipment malfunctions (radios, alarm systems, surveillance monitors). Assist in training new dispatchers and student employees as assigned. Stay updated on university safety protocols and participate in emergency drills and exercises. Maintain continuous awareness of Department of Public Safety personnel in the field or on special assignments. Stay updated on the latest emergency response protocols, security procedures, technology, University and Public Safety policies and procedures. Participate in ongoing training sessions to enhance skills related to Public Safety Dispatcher duties. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. This role is additional responsibility to Public Safety Officer duties which include responsibility of a dispatcher. Command Center Dispatchers, on occasion, will be required to work operational and special event overtime assignments. Command Center Dispatchers could be asked to shift hours for a period of time to meet the minimum requirements for the department. During emergency situations, such as snow storms, Command Center Dispatchers may be required to stay past their assigned tour/hours. Competencies, Education, Experience Clear, professional verbal and written communication. Strong attention to detail and ability to multitask under pressure. Ability to maintain composure and critical thinking in high-stress situations. Discretion and adherence to confidentiality and data privacy standards. Familiarity with public safety technologies (CAD, CCTV, radio systems). Excellent computer skills and be proficient in the use of emergency communications systems, including computer aided dispatch systems, multiple two-way radio systems, alarm receivers, video monitoring systems, access control systems, emergency mass notification systems, and telecommunications systems. Ability to remain on duty until relief is available and work weekends and different shifts as required. The Command Center is operated 24/7 including weekends and holidays and requires regular attendance and punctual employee presence. Customer service oriented and provide excellent customer service in all interactions. Required Education and Experience: High School diploma or equivalent required (GED). Prefer a minimum of 5 years’ security or dispatcher experience. Must obtain New York City Fire Department Certificate of Fitness (F-01) Fire Guard Impairment, to be obtained within six (6) months of employment; the certificate must be renewed by the Officer every two years and an updated copy provided to the Executive Director of Public Safety. Must obtain American Heart Association First Aid certification within ninety (90) days of employment. Must maintain certification while employed by St. John’s University. Candidate must possess and maintain a current New York Sate Security Guard License. Candidate must posess and maintain a valid Driver License from their state of residence. Candidate must be able to perform their responsibilities while wearing an N-95 respirator mask as mandated by OSHA regulations. Candidates must be able to work on all shifts, during various hours, including weekends and holidays. Preferred Education and Experience: Associates or Bachelors degree or equivalent experience. Bilingual skills are desirable. Supplemental Information Work Environment This position is performed in a secure command center environment. This position operates in a professional office environment and Command Center Dispatchers are required to use standard office equipment such as computers, printers, phones, copy machines, etc. Physical Demands Able to sit for extended periods and work shifts that include nights, weekends, and holidays. May occasionally lift or move equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. Environmental Conditions Must be able to work during emergencies, including pandemics, active shooter, weather emergencies, etc. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time Command Center Dispatchers may be assigned different shifts 24/7, including holidays and weekends. Typical hours range from: Day Shift: 7:00am-3:00pm Nigh Shift: 3:00pm-11:00pm Overnight Shift: 11:00am-7:00am Travel None required. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly rate for this position is $25.00. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer* St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5451866/simulation-virtual-reality-laboratory-technician": {
      "title": "Simulation & Virtual Reality Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Simulation & Virtual Reality Laboratory Technician Salary $55,000.00 - $65,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600055 Org College of Pharmacy and Health Sci Opening Date 08/18/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Simulation & Virtual Reality Laboratory Technician The Simulation & Virtual Reality Laboratory Technician works under the supervision of the College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Director of the Simulation Center to provide ongoing technical support for simulation and virtual reality delivery. This person is responsible for audio-visual (A/V) equipment evaluation, support, maintenance and setup; computer software support for simulation equipment as well as mannequins used in the simulation program. Major areas of responsibility include collaborating with the Director of the Simulation Center and College faculty to assist in the implementation and evaluation of technologies required for simulation programs using industry standards and established best practice standards; operating computer manikins, related operating software, programming needs and A/V equipment; and locating medical supplies needed to enhance delivery of simulation activities (e.g. IV supplies, pumps, dressings, etc.). Job Responsibilities Sets up simulation equipment and other learning technologies to meet the needs of faculty and students. Prepares supplies and equipment needed for simulation labs. Clean-up supplies, equipment, and mannequins once the simulation lab is complete. Restock simulation lab supplies/carts as needed for each lab. Operates and maintains computer hardware and audio-video recording systems. Handl es simulation equipment with the ability to follow medical aspects of scenario and make appropriate adjustments based on participant ’s actions. Aids faculty with human patient simulation labs and virtual reality labs including organization and preparation Identifies and implements solutions to problems related to simulation equipment, computer hardware, and software. Repairs and maintains equipment as required or initiates repairs for equipment under warranty. Communicates with manufacturers regarding maintenance, repairs, updates, and technology changes as directed by the Director of the Simulation Center. Co nveys both technical and non-technical matters effectively in person and in writing with a diverse population. Remains current with technical and professional skills by attending continuing education and training courses. Acquires and maintains skills and knowledge related to existing and newly acquired technologies in the College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences. Researches specifications for hardware and software products and must be aware of software licensing laws and requirements. Assists in maintaining reference materials for the simulation equipment and related audio-visual and computer hardware and software. Helps in maintaining an accurate inventory of simulation equipment including mannequins, hardware, and software. Trains faculty in operation of equipment as needed and develops quick-guide reference aids for faculty. Participates in College and University open houses, recruitment, student, and other College events as needed. Contributes effectively to a positive work environment that demonstrates and supports a learning-centered environment. Promotes and models a team approach in the conduct of daily operations within the College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences. Reinforces and maintains high ethical standards of conduct and procedures to assist in ensuring the security of the College's technology assets and data. Performs other duties as assigned by the Director of the Simulation Center. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in information technology, communications, related field or equivalent experience or Associate degree with five years of related work experience, preferably experience with healthcare simulation. Minimum of two years of IT support experience in the use of Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Windows Media, etc.) and have the ability to trouble shoot complex hardware/ software issues. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills, including a demonstrated ability to provide clear, concise directions and to communicate highly technical information to a technically diverse population. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs., with or without accommodations . Proven ability to maintain departmental records and facilities. Demonstrated ability to deal tactfully and effectively with administrators, faculty, students, sales representatives, and other personnel. Supplemental Information In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual salary range for this position is $55,000 - $65,000 . St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer.?All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5454426/senior-director-of-development-divisions-and-institutes": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Development, Divisions and Institutes",
      "description": "Senior Director of Development, Divisions and Institutes Salary $145,000.00 - $165,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600057 Org Institutional Advancement Opening Date 08/19/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Senior Director of Development, Divisions and Institutes will be responsible for major gift fundraising for university-wide initiatives, including Divisions, Institutes and non-academic departments, as determined by the Senior Vice President of Institutional Advancement. Primary responsibilities include developing and managing a portfolio of approximately 150 prospects/suspects, including alumni and friends of the University, and seeking, soliciting, and securing major gifts of $25,000 and above to the University. Job Responsibilities Manage a portfolio of approximately 150 prospects in support of the designated division, institute, and/or unit Develop and implement strategies for the cultivation, engagement, solicitation, and stewardship of major gift ($25,000 and above) prospects. Determine donor interest and develop and execute an individualized plan for each prospect. Solicit every prospect for an annual gift during each fiscal year, in addition to major and planned gifts as appropriate. Recommend suitable giving opportunities and prepare major gift proposals for specific initiatives and priorities. Participate in and advise on strategies that contribute to the development of a strong prospect pipeline. Work with other members of the Advancement team to appropriately engage assigned prospects in University activities. Participate as an active member of the prospect management process, including and especially identifying new prospects and developing strategies for those prospects. Actively engage with assigned prospects to follow up on, and secure pledge payments in a timely manner to support pledge fulfillment efforts. Ensure gift recognition occurs and acknowledgements are sent from the appropriate individuals in Advancement. Partner with division and institute leadership to identify funding priorities, translate programmatic needs into compelling cases for support, and align development efforts with strategic goals. Lead complex gift negotiations and close gifts that advance institutional priorities. Provide leadership and mentorship to development staff supporting divisions and institutes, as applicable. Partner with colleagues across development (annual giving, prospect research, donor relations, etc.) to maximize fundraising outcomes. Represent St. John’s University externally with donors, partners, and community stakeholders. Utilize data, analytics, and donor insights to inform strategy and optimize performance. Play a leadership role in capital campaigns and strategic initiatives tied to divisions and institutes. Contribute to messaging, case development, and donor engagement strategies. Collaborate on cross-functional initiatives that span multiple areas of the organization. Supervisory Responsibility Manage one Assistant Director of Development Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Competencies, Education, Experience Leadership & Professional Excellence : Demonstrated strength in leadership, project management, collaboration, analytical thinking, and stakeholder engagement. Relationship Building & Agility : Skilled at building strong relationships in donor-facing and professional settings; comfortable operating in social environments. Ability to manage multiple priorities and adapt quickly in a fast-paced, evolving environment. Communication & Organization : Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with strong organizational ability and attention to detail. Problem Solving & Judgment : Proven ability to think critically, resolve complex issues, work independently, and exercise sound professional judgment. Technical Proficiency : Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), including presentations, reporting, and data analysis. CRM & Development Systems Expertise : Experience with fundraising and CRM platforms such as Ellucian (Advance/Banner), Salesforce (Affinaquest, Ascend), or Blackbaud (CRM, Raiser’s Edge, NXT), with a focus on prospect management and pipeline tracking. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s Degree required. Minimum of 8–12 years of progressive experience in fundraising, advancement, or a related field. Minimum of 7+ years of one-on-one leadership ($1,500+) and/or major gift ($25,000+) solicitation experience. Minimum of 7+ years’ experience in Development, preferably in a Higher Education environment. Proven ability to build and manage relationships with senior leaders, donors, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated knowledge of development practices and principles and a track record of success in managing leadership or major gift prospects and in securing gifts. Demonstrated skill to work within a complex environment with strong capabilities in planning, organizing, and managing. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and peers in the Advancement area and with internal partners and external volunteers. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated interpersonal skills. Flexibility to travel, largely on a local/regional basis. Occasional weekend and evening work will be necessary, as well as occasional travel nationally. Affinity and commitment to the mission of St. John’s University. Preferred Education & Experience: Advanced degree (e.g., Master’s, MBA, or relevant field) preferred. Experience in complex, matrixed organizations such as healthcare systems, higher education, research institutions, or large nonprofit environments. Experience supporting or leading capital campaigns or large-scale fundraising initiatives. Familiarity with donor databases/CRMs and pipeline management tools. Experience working with faculty, or academic/institute program leadership. Supplemental Information Work Environment Working in the University Center, where Advancement is housed, as well as off campus, to visit with donors and prospects. Primary equipment includes the phone, laptop computer, and commercial printers. Physical Demands Prolonged periods of sitting and working at a computer, including virtual meetings and document preparation. Frequent verbal communication in person, over the phone, and via virtual platforms. Ability to travel regularly, including local and regional travel and occasional national travel; may involve extended periods of sitting, standing, or walking. Ability to attend and actively participate in events, which may require standing for extended periods. Occasional lifting and carrying of materials related to events or meetings (typically up to 10–15 pounds). Environmental Conditions Primarily office-based with a hybrid work environment (as applicable). Frequent attendance at events outside of standard business hours (evenings and weekends) to support donor engagement and stewardship. Work is fast-paced and deadline-driven, requiring the ability to manage multiple priorities and adapt to changing needs. Prolonged periods of sitting, working at a computer, and participating in virtual and in-person meetings. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time position with office hours matching University business day as well as off hours, attending events on nights and weekends as needed. Expectations are for flexibility as needed for events and fundraising opportunities outside of those hours. Travel There may be some travel involved, since the assigned prospects may not be local. Having a car is necessary for this position. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5468047/senior-associate-director-of-university-events-ceremonial": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Director of University Events -Ceremonial",
      "description": "Senior Associate Director of University Events -Ceremonial Salary $84,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600039 Org Office of University Events Opening Date 09/01/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Senior Associate Director serves as the primary event manager and planning lead for the University’s most visible institutional level events, including but not limited to ceremonial and academically affiliated events, including commencements, convocations, and other high-impact ceremonies and events. This role owns a defined portfolio of events and is responsible for the end-to-end planning, coordination, and execution of all events-related tasks, from early concept through delivery and post-event close-out. Working in close partnership with the Executive Director of the Office of University Events, the position shares accountability for event outcomes, execution readiness, and post-event assessment, consistent with the Office’s tiered portfolio model. Portfolio ownership includes discipline around scope, sequencing, and resourcing decisions, escalating matters of institutional risk or protocol exception to the Executive Director. The role translates academic tradition, institutional standards, and presidential priorities into disciplined, high-quality events and represents the Office with professionalism, judgment, and discretion in all internal Job Responsibilities Portfolio Ownership & Event Management • Serve as event manager for assigned events, including but not limited to ceremonial and academic such as commencements, convocations, and recognition ceremonies. • Act as the single point of coordination for all planning and execution-related tasks for assigned events. • Plan, integrate, and manage all event workstreams, ensuring tasks are identified, sequenced, and completed on schedule. • Ensure alignment with University goals, presidential priorities, and institutional strategy. Event Planning • Plan events that advance the priorities of the university while reflecting academic tradition, institutional protocol, and University standards. • Develop comprehensive planning materials for review with the Executive Director, including: o Event programs and planning proposals o Identification of key program participants, speakers, honorees, stage party, and leadership roles o Guest lists, seating charts, stage seating plans, recognition plans, and VIP protocols o Event run-of-show documents, scripts, cues, directions, and staffing assignments • Determine appropriate event locations (on- and off-campus) and submit recommendations for approval. • Conduct research and prepare statistical or summary information to support planning, proposals, and evaluations. Execution, Logistics & Vendor Coordination • Coordinate and oversee all logistical and operational elements of assigned events, including: o Venue preparation and space reservations o Staging, audiovisuals, accessibility, and security coordination o Vendor service requests, contracts, and floor plans o Catering coordination, menu development, and recommendations o Event staffing plans, including commencement host staffing and o Other event tasks as outlined in planning documents • Lead on-site execution, managing flow, timing, transitions, and real-time issue resolution. • Ensure all event materials and supplies are properly prepared, labeled, packed, and staged in advance. Commencement Planning & Committee Leadership • Serve as co-chair of the Commencement Committees. • Initiate and coordinate commencement committee schedules, planning timelines, and execution plans. • Develop agendas and planning materials for review and discussion with Executive Director. • Provide regular updates to the Executive Director to ensure alignment on priorities, readiness, and key decisions. Partnership & Collaboration • Work in close partnership with University leadership and, as needed, unit-based professionals to ensure clarity of roles, decision-rights, and shared accountability. • Support event objectives while maintaining institutional standards, protocol, and governance expectations. • Provide regular updates to the Executive Director to ensure alignment on priorities, readiness, and key decisions. Event Administration, Communications & Documentation • Prepare all event-related documents in accordance with Office procedures and governance standards. • Coordinate development of event communications and collateral in collaboration with MarCom. • Draft, review, and proof communications and printed materials for final approval. • Maintain reservation databases, as needed, seating charts, and master reply lists; execute mail merges and invitation distribution. • Maintain accurate electronic and hard-copy event files, including prior-year records, event binders, and shared folders. • Collaborate with the Assistant Director of Office Operations and Administration on event budgets and financial tracking. • Collaborate with Manager of Protocol and Event Systems Coordinator to improve efficiency and productivity as it relates to event tasks. Assessment, Reporting, and Continuous Improvement • Work with the Executive Director to define desired outcomes and measures of success for events. • Analyze the success of each event and identify opportunities for refinement and improvement in relation to strategic outcomes. • Prepare post-event assessments summarizing outcomes, feedback, and lessons learned. • Lead post-event evaluation, documentation, and reporting for assigned events. • Provide data, insights, and recommendations to support portfolio-level KPI assessment and continuous improvement efforts. Communication and Collaboration • Provide timely updates to the Executive Director and collaborate with University offices, event partners, schools, colleges, administrative units, and external partners to support effective planning and timely resolution of event-related issues. • Represent the Office of University Events with professionalism, discretion, and institutional awareness at all times. Assist with planning other high-level events and projects as needed. The role operates within institutional standards, protocols, and decision-making frameworks established by the Office and does not establish University-wide event policy or protocol. Competencies, Education, Experience • Deep understanding of academic ceremony, institutional protocol, and higher education culture. • Strong event planning and management skills in complex, high-visibility, ceremonial environments. • Demonstrated ability to plan, integrate, and manage large numbers of detailed, interdependent tasks. • Excellent follow-through and accountability; exercises independent judgment and sound decision-making. • Strong sense of urgency with a commitment to accuracy, quality, and timeliness. • Exceptional attention to detail; strong organizational and time-management skills. • Proven ability to manage multiple priorities and competing deadlines effectively. • Sound judgment and risk awareness, particularly in reputationally sensitive or ceremonial contexts. • Strong critical-thinking and problem-solving skills; resolves issues under pressure with professionalism and speed. • Maintains a calm, composed demeanor in high-stress and time-sensitive situations. • Ability to balance tradition, institutional standards, innovation, and operational practicality within governance frameworks. • Strong interpersonal and diplomatic skills; ability to build effective relationships with senior leadership, faculty, donors, alumni, students, and campus partners. • Clear, effective written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. • Ability to work independently in a fast-paced environment while functioning as a collaborative team member. • Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Access. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree required • 7–10 years of experience in ceremonial events, academic event planning, and/or institutional events, in protocol-driven environments • Demonstrated experience planning and executing large-scale, high-profile events • Strong organizational, coordination, and problem-solving skills Preferred Qualifications • Master’s degree in higher education administration, communications, public administration, hospitality, or a related field • Experience in a higher education or mission-driven institutional setting • Direct experience with commencements or major academic ceremonies Supervisory Responsibility No Additional Eligibility Qualifications N/A Other Duties This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive. Duties and responsibilities may change in response to institutional priorities and operational needs. Supplemental Information Work Environment This job operates in a professional office environment. This role uses standard office equipment such as personal computers, printers, etc. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is required to stand, move about, and communicate. The employee must lift or move up to 20-40 lbs. and perform moderate physical activity for event preparations and setups. Environmental Conditions N/A Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position in the office. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. in the office. This position requires long hours and weekend work for event preparation and on event days. Attendance at events, and evening and weekend work is required. Work hours may vary based on operational needs. Travel Local and tri-state travel is required for off-site events, site visits, and event-related errands and meetings. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5481702/postdoctoral-fellow-catastrophe-risk-and-insurance": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow – Catastrophe Risk and Insurance",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Fellow – Catastrophe Risk and Insurance Salary $70,000.00 - $100,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600074 Org Greenberg School of Risk Management Opening Date 09/14/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Postdoctoral Fellow will support the Institute for the Study of Catastrophe Risk and Resilience and the Greenberg School of Risk Management in advancing its research, education, and outreach mission. The Fellow will conduct independent and collaborative research on catastrophe risk management, risk mitigation and financing, and insurance solutions, and contribute to the organization of conferences and seminars. The Fellow will also teach one introductory course in Risk Management and Insurance. Job Responsibilities · Conduct independent and collaborative research on catastrophe risk management and insurance practices. · Produce high-quality working papers, journal articles, and practitioner-oriented publications. · Assist with organizing academic-industry conferences, micro-conferences, and research seminars. · Support student engagement through supervision of research assistants, and involvement in curricular enhancement. · Participate in community and industry outreach efforts to strengthen partnerships and disseminate research findings. · Maintain an active online presence for the Institute through contributions to its website and digital platforms. · Teach an Introductory Risk Management and Insurance course. Other Duties · Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change or be assigned as needed to support the mission of the Institute, the Greenberg School, and the Tobin College of Business. Supervisory Responsibility · None. Competencies, Education, Experience · Strong research skills in economics, finance, insurance, risk management, actuarial science, or related fields. · Ability to work collaboratively across disciplines and with industry partners. · Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. · Strong organizational and project management abilities. Required Education and Experience: · Ph.D. in economics, finance, risk management and insurance, actuarial science, or a closely related field (completed by the start date). · Demonstrated research expertise in catastrophe risk management, insurance, or resilience-related areas. · Significant data analysis and computer programing skills, e.g., Python, R. Preferred Education and Experience: · Experience with interdisciplinary collaboration and applied research. · Experience organizing academic conferences, workshops, or seminars. · Teaching or mentoring experience at the university level. Supplemental Information Work Environment · Operates in a professional office environment. This position is required to use standard office equipment such as personal computers, printers, etc. Physical Demands · While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand; move about; sit; to carry work and use computer and its controls; and communicate. Environmental Conditions · This work environment does not have any unique conditions, i.e. noise, fumes, odors, gases, dust, hazards, etc. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work · Full-time, 12-month appointment, renewable for up to two or three years, subject to performance and funding. · Typical schedule aligns with standard academic calendar; flexibility required for conferences, seminars and events. Travel · Occasional domestic and international travel to conferences, seminars, and research meetings. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5519460/security-application-administrator": {
      "title": "Security Application Administrator",
      "description": "Security Application Administrator Salary $72,700.00 - $81,800.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600096 Org Public Safety Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Security Application Specialist owns Tier 2 and Tier 3 technical operations for the University’s security technology platforms, including configuration, reliability monitoring, break-fix support, and controlled execution of complex changes. This role provides on-call response, maintains platform health and updates, supports integrations in steady state, and ensures technical work is documented and aligned with published standards and approvals. Job Responsibilities Core Responsibilities 1) Platform Configuration and Administration (30%) · Administer and configure security platforms (access control, video management, alarms, intercom/emergency phones, and related applications) using established standards and naming conventions. · Manage access levels, alarms, schedules, door and device programming, user permissions, analytics/AI settings where applicable, and system reporting parameters. · Maintain accurate configuration documentation and ensure changes are traceable through ticketing/change records. 2) Reliability, Health Monitoring, and Maintenance (20%) · Perform routine health checks, device status monitoring, and log reviews to identify issues before they impact operations. · Coordinate patching, upgrades, and maintenance windows; validate outcomes and document release notes/impacts. · Maintain integrations in steady state after project handoff and monitor integration health. 3) Incident Response and Break-Fix (Tier 2/3) (20%) · Respond to system incidents, outages, and priority issues; diagnose root cause and restore service quickly. · Coordinate escalations with vendors, integrators, IT, and Facilities as needed; document corrective actions. · Provide after-hours on-call coverage and follow published escalation pathways for major incidents. 4) Change Control and Complex Access Changes (15%) · Execute complex or sensitive access changes with documented approvals as required; escalate high-risk requests for Director review when needed. · Apply change controls for high-impact work (validation steps, back-out planning, and post-change monitoring). · Support periodic access and configuration audits and remediate findings. 5) Video and Data Exports (Execution) (5%) · Perform video export and technical evidence preparation when requested through approved workflows; maintain case/ticket tracking and chain-of-custody practices. · Support retention and release processes under Director-owned policy and governance. · Provide technical support for video playback, retrieval, and camera performance troubleshooting. 6) Documentation, SOPs, and Cross-Coverage (10%) · Develop and maintain technical SOPs, quick-reference guides, and troubleshooting playbooks for platforms and common issues. · Provide backup coverage for StormCard & Parking Office operations as needed, including escalations and complex access changes. · Participate in training and knowledge transfer to improve continuity and reduce single points of failure. Competencies, Education, Experience Minimum Qualifications · Bachelor’s degree in a related field (or equivalent combination of education and experience). · Progressive experience administering security technology platforms, service ticket resolution, and technical troubleshooting. · Working knowledge of access control and IP video systems, including device programming concepts and operational impacts. · Vendor/platform certifications (or ability to obtain) in access control and video platforms (e.g., Lenel/OnGuard, Avigilon/Alta Video, or similar).. · Demonstrated understanding of networking fundamentals (IP addressing, VLAN concepts, connectivity troubleshooting). · Experience with Windows administration basics and vendor client tools; ability to document and follow change controls. · Ability to participate in an on-call rotation and work after-hours for planned maintenance or urgent incidents. Preferred Qualifications · Working knowledge of SQL queries and reporting for platform administration. · Experience with scripting/automation for reporting or integrations (PowerShell, Python, or similar). · ITIL or comparable incident/change management training. Supplemental Information Work Environment and Requirements · Work is performed in an office and field environment with periodic visits to buildings, closets, and system rooms for troubleshooting and coordination. · May require lifting/carrying equipment and working in utility spaces as needed for oversight and troubleshooting. · Employment is contingent on successful completion of background screening consistent with University policy. · May require some installation or servicing of parts. How This Role Will Be Measured (Example Performance Indicators) · Mean time to acknowledge and mean time to restore for incidents. · Ticket closure rate and backlog age; repeat-issue reduction. · Patch and update compliance; maintenance success rate. · After-hours response performance and escalation effectiveness. · Change quality (reduced change-induced incidents and rework). *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5519490/physician-assistant-educator": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant Educator",
      "description": "Physician Assistant Educator Salary $80.00 Hourly Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600099 Org College of Pharmacy and Health Sci Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division/Department Information The College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences is seeking qualified Physician Assistants to serve as part-time, hourly laboratory educators in the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Program. Job Responsibilities Under the direct supervision of the assigned course coordinator, the laboratory educator will support the delivery of hands-on instruction, student practice, clinical skills development, and formative feedback in one or more of the following laboratory courses: Anatomy, Physiology, and Pathophysiology Laboratory · Facilitate the identification and application of clinically relevant anatomical structures. · Reinforce normal physiology and the mechanisms underlying common disease processes. · Assist students in connecting anatomy, physiology, and pathophysiology to clinical findings and patient presentations. · Guide students in the appropriate use of anatomical models, specimens, digital resources, imaging, or other laboratory materials. · Support case-based activities that integrate foundational science with clinical practice. Health History and Physical Diagnosis Laboratory · Demonstrate and supervise the performance of complete and focused histories and physical examinations. · Teach appropriate examination techniques, patient positioning, draping, communication, and documentation. · Observe students performing clinical skills and provide feedback regarding technique, organization, accuracy, professionalism, and patient comfort. · Assist with physical examination skills assessments, practical examinations, or structured clinical encounters as directed by the course coordinator. · Reinforce recognition of normal and abnormal examination findings. Surgical Procedures Laboratory · Demonstrate and supervise procedural skills within the scope of Physician Assistant education. · Reinforce sterile technique, universal precautions, procedural safety, and appropriate disposal of sharps and biohazardous materials. · Provide instruction in procedures that may include suturing, knot tying, wound care, local anesthesia techniques, surgical instrument identification and handling, sterile preparation and draping, and other assigned clinical procedures. · Monitor the safe and appropriate use of procedural equipment, supplies, task trainers, and simulation materials. · Provide immediate corrective feedback during procedural practice. Clinical Mastery in Organ Systems: Problem-Based Learning Laboratory · Facilitate small-group, case-based learning under the guidance of the course coordinator. · Guide students through the development of differential diagnoses, diagnostic plans, treatment plans, and patient education. · Encourage evidence-based clinical reasoning and integration of material across organ systems and disciplines. · Ask focused questions that promote student analysis without taking over the problem-solving process. · Support collaborative learning, professional communication, teamwork, and student participation. · Identify significant knowledge gaps or performance concerns and communicate them to the course coordinator. Responsibilities Under the supervision and direction of the course coordinator, the laboratory educator will: · Attend and provide instruction during assigned laboratory sessions. · Review the applicable laboratory objectives, instructional materials, procedures, and faculty guidance before each assigned session. · Prepare sufficiently to teach and demonstrate the skills or concepts assigned by the course coordinator. · Provide small-group and individual instruction to Physician Assistant students. · Demonstrate clinical, diagnostic, physical examination, procedural, and clinical reasoning skills using current professional standards. · Observe students as they practice assigned skills and provide timely, constructive, and consistent feedback. · Reinforce appropriate patient communication, professionalism, infection-control practices, patient safety, and clinical decision-making. · Help maintain a respectful, inclusive, and psychologically safe learning environment. · Ensure that students follow laboratory safety procedures and instructions regarding the appropriate use of equipment, supplies, task trainers, models, standardized patients, or other educational resources. · Assist with skills practice, check-offs, practical examinations, simulations, or other student assessments when assigned by the course coordinator. · Apply established evaluation criteria, checklists, or rubrics consistently when participating in student assessment. · Promptly communicate student performance or safety concerns to the course coordinator. · Maintain student confidentiality and comply with all University policies, including requirements related to FERPA, nondiscrimination, professional conduct, safety, and academic integrity. · Perform other directly related instructional laboratory activities assigned by the course coordinator within the scope of this hourly position. This is an hourly instructional position and carries no routine administrative responsibilities (e.g., course coordination, student advisement, committee service, accreditation responsibilities, or other administrative duties). Appointments and work schedules are based on course needs, educator availability, qualifications, and relevant clinical experience. The number of assigned hours may vary by semester and is not guaranteed. Competencies, Education, Experience Required Qualifications · Graduation from an ARC-PA-accredited Physician Assistant program. · Current NCCPA certification. · Current, unencumbered New York State Physician Assistant license or eligibility for New York State licensure. · Current clinical knowledge and competence relevant to the assigned laboratory content. · Ability to demonstrate clinical and procedural skills accurately and safely. · Effective oral communication and interpersonal skills. · Ability to provide constructive feedback to graduate-level students. · Ability to work collaboratively and follow the instructional plan established by the course coordinator. · Commitment to maintaining student confidentiality, academic integrity, professionalism, and an inclusive learning environment. Preferred Qualifications · At least two years of clinical experience as a practicing Physician Assistant. · Current clinical practice experience in a field relevant to the assigned laboratory. · Prior teaching, precepting, simulation, or clinical skills laboratory experience. · Experience working with Physician Assistant or other health-professions students. · Experience facilitating small-group or problem-based learning. · Current BLS certification; ACLS certification may be preferred for certain instructional assignments. · Familiarity with contemporary clinical practice guidelines and evidence-based medicine. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5463635/testing-coordinator": {
      "title": "Testing Coordinator",
      "description": "Testing Coordinator Salary $55,000.00 - $61,850.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600066 Org Office of Student Affairs Opening Date 09/29/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Reporting to the Director of Student Accessibility Services, the Testing Coordinator plays a central role in making sure students with approved accommodations receive equitable, well-organized testing support. The Testing Coordinator oversees the planning, scheduling, and administration of accommodated exams for students registered with Student Accessibility Services. The role ensures that testing accommodations are implemented accurately, confidentially, and in alignment with university policies and federal disability laws. The coordinator serves as a key liaison among students, faculty, and staff to support an accessible and inclusive academic environment. The SAS is housed within the Department of Student Wellness at St. John’s University. The Department of Student Wellness engages in an integrated approach to wellness that fosters collaboration between Student Health Services, Wellness Education and Prevention, Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS), Student Accessibility Services (SAS), Campus Recreation, and Sexual Violence Outreach, Awareness, and Response (SOAR). Job Responsibilities Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Manage daily testing operations including scheduling, arranging proctors, and coordinating exams for students receiving accommodations such as extended time, reduced-distraction environments, assistive technology, or alternative formats. Coordinate the use of alternative testing formats including readers, scribes, assistive technology, and accessible materials as needed. Support students by providing clear instructions, maintaining a welcoming testing environment, and addressing questions related to testing procedures and accommodations. Hire, onboard and supervise part-time testing proctors and student workers. Communicate regularly with faculty to request exam materials, clarify testing instructions, confirm accommodation needs, and ensure timely return of completed exams. Maintain secure exam handling by implementing a system to track receipt, storage, administration, and return of all exam materials while upholding strict confidentiality. Maintain detailed records of exams administered, incidents, and accommodation usage; prepare reports for departmental assessment. Implement testing accommodations approved by Student Accessibility Services staff, ensuring accommodations such as extended time, reduced-distraction environments, assistive technology, readers, or scribes are administered accurately. Support broader disability services initiatives, participate in staff meetings, and assist during peak accommodation periods. Competencies, Education, Experience Demonstrate subject matter expertise with assistive technology and Section 504 and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and with other federal and state regulations concerning students with disabilities especially as it pertains to the implementation of testing accommodations. Keen attention to detail, ensuring accuracy in scheduling, documentation, and exam handling. Ability to solve problems and navigate last-minute changes, conflicts, or unexpected testing needs. Understands the importance of access and inclusion in academic settings. Manages high-volume testing periods with professionalism. Works closely with faculty, students, and colleagues across campus. Supervisory Responsibility: Team of 3-5 student workers, part-time proctors and GAs Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in education, psychology, counseling, disability services, or a related field. Experience working in higher education, disability services, testing centers, or student support roles. Experience administering exams or coordinating academic accommodations Knowledge of accessible technology (screen readers, speech-to-text tools, alternative formats). Supervisory experience with student workers or proctors. Ability to work effectively with diverse populations, including students with disabilities, faculty, and staff, Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion. Familiarity with disability law (ADA, Section 504) and accommodation practices. Comfort with technology, including scheduling systems, learning management systems, and assistive technology tools. Reports to: Director, Student Accessibility Services Department of Student Wellness Division of Student Affairs Supplemental Information Work Environment: This role operates primarily in an office environment within St. John’s University’s Office of Student Accessibility Services. Interaction involves frequent contact with students experiencing varying degrees of mental health challenges. Work is typically performed in a confidential, private setting. The role is based in an office environment within a student services or accessibility services suite. The space typically includes: A reception or student-facing area Private or semi-private testing rooms Quiet, reduced-distraction spaces Storage areas for secure exam materials Workstations equipped with scheduling software and assistive technology tools The atmosphere is professional, calm, and centered on supporting equitable access for students with disabilities. Physical Demands: Ability to remain in a stationary position (sitting/standing) for extended periods while conducting evaluations and follow up visits. Frequent use of computers, phones, and medical records systems. Light physical activity such as walking between campus locations may be required. Environmental Conditions: Standard clinical/office environment with minimal exposure to adverse conditions. Some exposure to emotionally charged situations when working with students in crisis. Requires maintaining a calm, professional demeanor in stressful circumstances. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work: Full time; specific schedule to be determined in collaboration with the Director of Student Accessibility Services. Flexible hours with potential for early morning testing administration, evenings and/or weekend availability during peak times. Travel: None *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5509059/sjc-physics-adjunct-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "SJC Physics Adjunct Assistant Professor",
      "description": "SJC Physics Adjunct Assistant Professor Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600089 Org Physics Opening Date 10/07/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary Division/Department Information The Department of Physics is committed to providing an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students, faculty and staff from all backgrounds and thrive. Our department and faculty are dedicated to students' success through physics education in a liberal arts Catholic and Vincentian College. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities The Department of Physics is seeking candidates for the position of non-tenure track, Adjunct Assistant Professor. The successful candidate should have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. The successful candidate will: Teach one 2-hour labs and one 1-hour recitation each week Deliver instruction clearly, efficiently, and professionally in lab demonstration and recitation practice Assess student performance through lab reports, recitation quizzes, etc. and submit grades in accordance with university policies Manage and update course materials through Canvas as required by the department Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications Ph.D. in Physics, Applied Physics, Engineering, or closely related area. Previous undergraduate teaching experience is preferred. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Supplemental Information Application Process Interested candidates should submit a curriculum vitae (or résumé), statement of teaching, and the names and contact information of three professional references by Nov 1, 2026. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Gen Long, Acting-Chair of Department of Physics, at longg@stjohns.edu. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the minimum credit hour rate for this position is $1,906. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5519516/training-officer": {
      "title": "Training Officer",
      "description": "Training Officer Salary $55,000.00 - $61,850.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600100 Org Public Safety Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Training Officer is responsible for the development, implementation, coordination, and evaluation of all training programs for the Department of Public Safety at St. John's University. This position serves as the department's primary subject matter expert for training, professional development, onboarding, regulatory compliance, and operational readiness. The Training Officer oversees the classroom and field training of all full-time and part-time Public Safety Officers. As operational needs require, the Training Officer may also be assigned to a regular duty shift or to staff special events and incidents. Job Responsibilities Develop, implement, and maintain a comprehensive Public Safety Officer Training Program. Create annual, quarterly, and monthly training plans. Plan, schedule, coordinate, and evaluate all in-service training programs. Develop lesson plans, training materials, practical exercises, field training guides, and training assessments. Maintain a department-wide training calendar and training records management system. New Hire Orientation and Field Training Provide comprehensive onboarding and orientation training for all newly hired full-time and per diem Public Safety Officers. Instruct new officers on university policies and procedures, the Public Safety Department Manual, report writing, customer service, access control systems, radio communications, fire safety systems, residence hall operations, and emergency response procedures. Provide a comprehensive campus orientation and operational familiarization program. Operational Cross-Training Ensure all officers receive training and exposure to Dispatch Operations, CCTV Monitoring, Patrol Operations, Access Control Systems, Emergency Communications, Fire Safety Systems, Residence Hall Operations, and Special Event Operations. In-Service Training and Regulatory Compliance Assist in planning and coordinating all mandatory annual in-service training. Coordinate CPR, AED, First Aid, emergency preparedness, and emergency response training. Ensure compliance with all applicable training requirements. Certification and License Management Track and maintain New York State Security Guard registrations, Fire Guard certifications, CPR/AED certifications, First Aid certifications, driver authorizations, and all required departmental credentials and licenses. Campus Collaboration Work collaboratively with Human Resources, Student Affairs, Residence Life, Athletics, Facilities Services, Risk Management, Emergency Management personnel, and other campus partners to coordinate training initiatives. Competencies, Education, Experience Competencies Excellent written and verbal communication skills; strong organizational abilities; curriculum development and instructional expertise; leadership and mentoring capabilities; outstanding customer service skills; strong recordkeeping and compliance management skills. Required Qualifications Minimum eight years of experience in public safety, law enforcement, security, or a related field; minimum three years of training and instructional experience; valid New York State Security Guard License; valid Driver License. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's Degree; previous higher education public safety experience; CPR/AED Instructor certification; experience managing training programs and regulatory compliance. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5522153/assistant-director-public-safety-operations": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Public Safety Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Public Safety Operations Salary $83,600.00 - $94,050.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600098 Org Public Safety Opening Date 10/20/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Assistant Director, Public Safety Operations serves as the Queens campus operational owner and the event security authority, ensuring consistent staffing standards, inspections, performance management, and risk-tiered event planning. This role oversees daily operational deployment and redeployments, supervises operational standards and coaching, and approves event security plans and staffing models within delegated authority Job Responsibilities Core Responsibilities 1) Queens Daily Operations, Staffing Coverage, and Redeployment (25%) • Manage day-to-day Queens campus operations, including post coverage, minimum staffing compliance, deployment adjustments, and operational issue resolution. • Redeploy resources in response to changing conditions, incident activity, staffing shortages, or emergent safety needs while maintaining core coverage standards. • Coordinate execution expectations with dispatch and field supervisors to support consistent service delivery. Manage and approve time and attendance for Public Safety personnel, including Sergeants and, at times, Officers. Manage and oversee the Public Safety fleet, radios, and other operational resources, including but not limited to signage and traffic materials. 2) Leadership, Supervision, and Performance Management (25%) • Provide direct supervision, coaching, and performance expectations for assigned supervisors/officers and event-related supervisory staff. • Align coaching, evaluations, and accountability practices to operational standards, professionalism, and community engagement expectations. • Address performance issues, recurring deficiencies, and training needs through documented follow-up and coordination with leadership/HR as appropriate. 3) Inspections, Quality of Execution, and Corrective Follow-Through (20%) • Conduct frequent and random post inspections to verify staffing, readiness, professionalism, and adherence to post expectations. • Document inspection results, identify recurring gaps, and implement corrective actions or coaching to reduce repeat deficiencies. • Track inspection outcomes and use trends to improve operational reliability. 4) Emergency Response Coordination and Command-Level Updates (20%) • Support emergency response coordination on the Queens campus and provide command\u0002level updates to leadership as required. • Serve in an operational leadership role during major incidents and higher-risk events, coordinating internal and external partners as needed. • Support after-action review inputs and operational refinement following significant incidents or events. 5) Stakeholder Coordination, Event Pipeline Review, and Reporting (10%) • Coordinate with Student Affairs, Athletics, Conference Services, Residence Life, Facilities, and Technology partners on event planning inputs and execution readiness. • Lead recurring event pipeline reviews and operations status discussions with stakeholders. • Provide concise updates on staffing, inspections, event readiness, and operational trends to leadership. Competencies, Education, Experience Minimum Qualifications • Bachelor's degree required; equivalent combination of education and progressively responsible experience may be considered per University practice. • Significant experience in public safety/security operations, law enforcement, campus safety, or a comparable operational leadership environment. • Supervisory experience with responsibility for staffing, deployment, coaching, and performance management. • Experience planning or overseeing events, special operations, or risk-based operational deployments. • Demonstrated ability to make sound operational decisions under pressure and coordinate across multiple stakeholders. • Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to document plans, inspections, and follow-up actions. Preferred Qualifications • Experience in higher education public safety and campus event security planning. • Experience with incident command principles, emergency operations coordination, and after\u0002action processes. • Familiarity with dispatch coordination, staffing models, and post inspection/quality assurance practices. • Experience using scheduling, incident reporting, and event planning tools/systems. Supplemental Information Work Environment and Requirements • Work is performed in both office and field environments, including extensive campus movement and outdoor activity during events. • Role requires evening, weekend, and holiday availability based on operational and event needs. • This position may be designated essential personnel and may require response during emergencies, severe weather, or campus disruptions. How This Role Will Be Measured (Example Performance Indicators) • Daily minimum staffing/coverage compliance rate and response to redeployment needs. • Event plan on-time submission and approval rate. • Post inspection compliance rate and repeat-deficiency trend. • Operational overtime trend versus baseline/approved plan (if tracked). • Event/operations after-action completion and corrective follow-through for major events. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5524437/department-of-core-studies-science-inquiry-adjunct-instructor": {
      "title": "Department of Core Studies Science Inquiry Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Department of Core Studies Science Inquiry Adjunct Instructor Salary See Position Description Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Part-Time Faculty Job Number 202600105 Org Department of Core Studies Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary About the Position The primary responsibility for this position is teaching the university science core during the daytime hours on campus. The needs of the department will determine the number of sections to be assigned to adjunct faculty. For more information about the course, please visit the Department for Core Studies? website . Job Responsibilities Most classes are held in-person on campus (at the address:?8000 Utopia Parkway, Queens, NY 11439), but some classes may be online, synchronously or asynchronously. For asynchronous classes, a specific training certificate is required. Competencies, Education, Experience Qualifications Applicants should possess at least a master’s degree in a natural science-based discipline such as biology, chemistry, physics or similar fields. Strong skills in student engagement are required. Evidence of experience teaching a general science course to non-majors is preferred. It is expected that the position will be renewable. High-quality teaching is essential for the renewal of the position for the subsequent years. The initial rank depends on the highest degree of the candidate and the availability of the documented experience. The hire-on rate is a minimum of $1,803.00 per credit for candidates without Ph.D. and $1,906.00 per credit for candidates with a Ph.D. Supplemental Information Application Process Please apply?online?and include the following: A cover letter explaining your interest in the position, in our department and in doing the work described in the “Responsibilities” above. A Curriculum Vitae. A teaching statement expressing a philosophy of teaching and/or describing the candidate’s ability to engage non-major students in learning about the scientific process. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the minimum credit hour rate for this position is $1,803-$1,906. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5519473/public-safety-events-supervisor": {
      "title": "Public Safety Events Supervisor",
      "description": "Public Safety Events Supervisor Salary $72,700.00 - $81,800.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600097 Org Public Safety Opening Date 10/16/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Events Supervisor is responsible for supervising internal and external University events. A critical function of the Public Safety Event Supervisor is his/her attendance at meetings with the planning members of the Athletics Department, Student life (Greek Life), Conference Services and Public Safety. The Events Supervisor is responsible for reviewing and evaluating the nine thousand passes generated yearly for both internal and external events here on campus. The Events Supervisor must evaluate how many Public Safety Officers are required to keep each event as safe as humanly possible while maintaining a balance within the University’s budget constraints. Job Responsibilities Supervise the events on campus to include both internal University events and outside events. This will include preparing the roll calls for the events and assigning the personnel scheduled to work that event. • Schedule and call the Per Diems for events, patrol, shuttle and Resident Village coverage. • Supervise and monitor the Per Diems for uniforms, appearance, customer service skills and communication skills. When necessary prepare disciplinary records for problematic Per Diems. • Notify the Assistant Director, Administration & Events by email on all payroll changes, disciplinary problems and all other pertinent information. • After every event email the Director, Public Safety and Assistant Director, Administration & Events with a critique of the event including any problems or issues, attendance, name of the event and all other pertinent information. • During events where any problems or issues necessitate making notifications to an outside agency or other administrators within the University, notify Chief of Public Safety and Director, Public Safety immediately by cell phone. • Backfill for the Supervisors assigned to steady tour when they are on vacation and in emergency situations. Backfill for Supervisors when no events are scheduled to cover. • Monitor all campus calendars to make sure they are up to date on events and activities. Make sure the Per Diem Officers are continually instructed at roll calls before the events begin. Also make sure that the Per Diems are communicating the correct information to the University community. • Supervise all department reports prepared by the Per Diems for accuracy. Make sure the Per Diems are instructed on accuracy and neatness. If Per Diems require special instruction to assure that the reports are accurate and completed correctly, provide them with the necessary time. • Continously reaffirm the policy and procedures of the department; make sure the Per Diems are updated and instructed. • Continually assess customer service via dialogue with Public Safety personnel and feedback from the community Competencies, Education, Experience • Bachelor’s degree preferred • 5-10 years of experience in security and/or Police environment preferred. • Proficiency with MS Word, Excel, Outlook, Banner, UIS • Excellent customer service skills are required • Ability to multitask • Attention to detail • Excellent verbal and written communication skills • Ability to exercise high level of discretion, good judgment, and professionalism • Capacity to work in a fast-paced, unpredictable environment • Must be highly flexible and accessible after normal business hours. Schedule will be pre\u0002approved by Assistant Director, Administration & Events. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply"
